      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4326120336": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "At ClickUp, we're building the future of work: the first truly converged AI workspace unifying tasks, docs, chat, calendar, and enterprise search, all supercharged by context-driven AI. We are an AI-native company. Every team member is expected to leverage AI daily, and we evaluate AI fluency as part of our hiring process. Join us and help redefine what's possible. 🚀\nCome join the Hierarchy Squad to build and optimize a set of tier 1 services that are at the core of ClickUp’s all-in-one productivity platform! Hierarchy owns the ClickUp filesystem that is at foundation of everything we build. We are searching for passionate engineers with exceptional critical thinking skills and technical prowess to help maintain, develop and scale high throughput services to support the company through accelerated growth. The ideal candidate will find the idea of architecting distributed systems that are reliable and highly performant exciting, has a knack for debugging and writing complex code and is excited by the challenge of building and maintaining a platform that every team in the company integrates with. Our key technologies include Typescript, Postgres, Kafka, NestJS running on Amazon Web Services. If this sounds interesting to you, we'd love to have you join our team!\nResponsibilities:\nDevelop and maintain robust, scalable backend systems using Node.js (Express and NestJS).\nCollaborate with engineers, designers, and product managers to drive projects forward.\nTune and optimize database queries for maximum efficiency and performance.\nOptimize and improve existing code for better performance and user experience.\nTroubleshoot and debug issues, ensuring smooth operations.\nShare your knowledge and expertise to foster a culture of learning and growth.\nRequirements:\n8+ years of professional experience building backend services for SaaS products.\nProven track record of building and scaling backend systems.\nExpertise in relational database query optimizations (prefer PostgreSQL).\nExtensive background working with databases (SQL and NoSQL) and data modeling.\nStrong understanding of RESTful API design and implementation.\nExperience with agile development methodologies (Scrum, Kanban, etc.).\nFamiliarity with version control systems like Git.\nExcellent problem-solving skills and a passion for tackling challenges.\nStrong communication skills, as collaboration is key to our success.\nExperience with microservices architecture and containerization (Docker, Kubernetes).\nPreferred Qualifications:\nFamiliarity with frontend technologies (Angular, React, Vue).\nProfessional experience with NodeJs, Express, and NestJS\nWhat we offer:\nCompetitive salary and benefits package.\nRemote work options.\nA supportive, dynamic, and fast-paced work environment.\nThe opportunity to make a meaningful impact on a rapidly growing company.\nOpportunities for personal and professional growth.\nEqual Opportunity Employer\nClickUp is an Equal Opportunity Employer, and qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin.\nPrivacy Notice\nClickUp collects and processes personal data in accordance with applicable data protection laws. You can find further details by viewing our Global Candidate Privacy Notice.\nIf you are a Philippine Job Applicant, please also see our Philippine Data Privacy Notice for further details.\nVisa Sponsorship\nPlease note we are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa for roles outside of engineering and product at this time. Sponsorship for engineering and product roles is not guaranteed, but is instead based on the business needs for that specific role at that time. Please reach out to the recruiter with any questions.\nFraud Alert\nClickUp Talent Acquisition will only initiate contact via an @ clickup.com email or through our official careers portal on clickup.com . We will never request fees, payments, or sensitive personal information. Please disregard any offers received outside these channels and report them to support@clickup.com.\nAI Processing Notice\nClickUp may use artificial intelligence and machine learning technologies to help review and screen candidates' employment applications against role-related criteria. These tools support, but do not replace, human decision‑making. If you have questions or need an accommodation in the recruitment process, please contact us at AskPeople@ClickUp.com.\nCompensation Range: $200K - $250K",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4370759275": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Type\nFull-time\nDescription\nSpatial Front, Inc. (SFI), a two-time USAToday Top Workplaces awardee and Washington Top Workplaces honoree, is seeking a Full Stack Developer with strong backend and full-stack experience and recent NodeJS expertise to support mission-critical applications in an Agile environment. This role focuses on building, enhancing, and maintaining modern cloud-native systems with an emphasis on performance, scalability, and reliability.\nPrimary Responsibilities\nDesign, build, and maintain APIs within a serverless AWS environment\nCollaborate with stakeholders, project managers, QA, and development teams\nDevelop, test, and deploy high-quality, maintainable code using modern testing frameworks (Mocha/Chai)\nImprove system performance, scalability, and availability across complex applications\nParticipate in Agile/Scrum ceremonies and iterative development cycles\nSupport ongoing feature enhancements, UI improvements, and system updates\nRequirements\nRequired Qualifications\nBachelor’s degree in a related field (required)\n5+ years of backend and/or full-stack development experience\nProficiency in NodeJS, TypeScript, and JavaScript\nHands-on experience with AWS services, including:\nAWS Lambda\nAPI Gateway\nCloudFormation\nS3, SNS, SQS\nExperience with ElasticSearch\nStrong experience working in Agile/Scrum environments\nPreferred Experience\nExperience supporting federal or government technology programs\nAdditional Information\nTo meet the clearance requirements for this opportunity, the candidate must be authorized to work in the United States\nAbility to obtain and maintain a Public Trust clearance (includes fingerprinting and background investigation)\nAll candidates will be subject to a complete background check, including, but not limited to, Criminal History, Education Verification, Professional Certification Verification, Verification of Previous Employment, and Credit History.\nOther Information\nThis position is fully remote.\nFor information on SFI's benefits, please visit http://www.spatialfront.com/pages/career.html\nThis is a full-time W2 position.\nThe salary range for this position is between $80,000-$120,000 Annually\nPlease no agencies, third parties, or corp-to-corp.\nSpatial Front Inc. is an Equal-opportunity Employer; all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran.\nSpatial Front Inc. participates in E-Verify.\nSalary Description\n$80,000 – $120,000 annually",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4410599079": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Storytelling is, and will always be, the heart of what we do at Skydance.\nOur vision is to build a thriving entertainment ecosystem where stories and worlds are imagined, brought to life and experienced. We create for every age and audience, anchored by the strength of our content and experiences and the depth of our connection with fans. We are creator-first, audience-focused, tech-forward, globally scaled.\nHere, you’ll work with talented teams that move fast, think boldly and collaborate with purpose to deliver results. We aim high, champion the best ideas and win together, earning the trust of our employees, creators, partners and audiences every day.\nIf you’re energized by the opportunity to help build the next-generation global media and entertainment company powered by creativity and technology, we’d be thrilled to welcome you aboard. LET’S GO!\nOverview And Responsibilities\nThe Applied Machine Learning Group is seeking a Software Engineer to build and scale systems that power\ncontent understanding, metadata enrichment, and personalization across Paramount's global content\ncatalog. In this role, you will work on the core infrastructure and internal tools that enable high-\nquality metadata ingestion and curation directly impacting content discovery,\nrecommendations, and user experience across Paramount's streaming portfolio.\nThis is a highly cross-functional role at the intersection of content, data, and machine learning,\npartnering closely with ML engineers, product teams, and data stakeholders to bring metadata-driven\nexperiences to life.\nThe ideal candidate will be:\nEnthusiastic about spanning the full lifecycle of a content data system from ingest and\nenrichment through deployment, monitoring, and downstream delivery\nInvested in going beyond moving data to understanding it; developing domain-level\nfamiliarity with the content catalog, and how data quality issues upstream affect systems\ndownstream\nCommitted to continuous improvement; takes ownership of feature implementation,\nplans for future maintainability\nSkilled at partnering with Product to translate evolving content strategy into concrete\nengineering decisions; asking clarifying questions and iterating toward well-defined\nsolutions under ambiguity\nCollaborative across engineering teams; working with upstream providers and\ndownstream consumers to define integration contracts, and ensuring the sequencing of\nchanges so that features ship cohesively\nEager to leverage AI agents in the software development process for understanding\ncode, troubleshooting, developing new features, and fixing issues\nResponsibilities Include:\nMetadata Ingestion & Enrichment\nDesign, build, and maintain backend services that support content understanding,\nmetadata modeling, and enrichment workflows\nContribute to systems that process and manage metadata for a large-scale, global\ncontent catalog\nBackend Services & Data Modeling\nMaintain and expand the API layer and data models across two provider contexts\n(Paramount+ and PlutoTV) as the codebase converges toward a unified multi-tenant\narchitecture\nUphold engineering quality through test coverage, code reviews, and consistent\napplication of coding standards\nInternal Tooling & Curation\nSupport editorial curation workflows that feed the personalization experience, ensuring\ncurators have the tooling and data quality needed to make effective content decisions\nBasic Qualifications\n3+ years of professional software engineering experience\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent experience\nStrong proficiency in a Python web API and ORM framework (Django/ORM/DRF\npreferred)\nKnowledge of cloud infrastructure including managed databases, object storage, and\ncontainer orchestration (GCP, AWS, or Azure)\nAPI design with backwards compatibility across multiple consumer teams\nRelational data modeling for transactional systems\nExperience building data engineering pipelines, including best practices like defensive\ncoding at ingestion boundaries, instrumentation to surface anomalies early, and\nawareness of data drift so that quality issues are caught before they propagate\ndownstream\nAdditional Qualifications\nDjango and Django REST Framework for production backend applications\nGoogle Cloud Platform: Cloud SQL, BigQuery, Cloud Storage, Secret Manager, GKE\nGoogle Cloud Pub/Sub subscriber/publisher patterns\nElasticsearch index management, full-text search, mapping updates\nExperience building content metadata management systems\nExposure to personalization, recommendation systems, or ML-adjacent platforms\nExperience working in event-driven architectures, designing systems around async\npipelines\nParamount Streaming, a division within Paramount Global, is the home to the company's direct-to-consumer services spanning free and paid in the form of Pluto TV and Paramount+. Pluto TV is the global leader in free ad-supported TV, delivering more than 1,400 global channels and an extensive library of streaming content, including live and original channels. Paramount+, digital subscription video-on-demand and live streaming service, combines live sports, breaking news, and A Mountain of Entertainment™. Paramount+ features an expansive library of original series, hit shows and popular movies across every genre from world-renowned brands and production studios, including SHOWTIME®.\nAdditional Information\nHiring Salary Range: $110,400.00 - 165,600.00.\nThe hiring salary range for this position applies to New York, California, Colorado, Washington state, and most other geographies. Starting pay for the successful applicant depends on a variety of job-related factors, including but not limited to geographic location, market demands, experience, training, and education. The benefits available for this position include medical, dental, vision, 401(k) plan, life insurance coverage, disability benefits, tuition assistance program and PTO or, if applicable, as otherwise dictated by the appropriate Collective Bargaining Agreement. This position is bonus eligible.\nWhat We Offer :\nAttractive compensation and comprehensive benefits packages. Check out our full list of benefits here.\nGenerous paid time off.\nComplimentary subscriptions to HBO Max, Paramount+, and other Skydance streaming services and digital news products.\nRobust employee engagement opportunities, including access to exclusive screenings and events, speaker series, volunteer activities and more.\nSkydance is an equal opportunity employer (EOE)\nWe embrace the opportunity to build a workforce that reflects a wide array of perspectives, backgrounds and experiences. Being an equal opportunity employer means that we take seriously our responsibility to consider qualified candidates on the basis of merit. In line with the laws of the country or region in which the role is based, this includes consideration without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, religion or belief, sex, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, marital status, pregnancy, parenthood, physical or mental disability, genetic information, military or protected veteran status, union status or any other category protected by applicable law.\nIf you are a qualified individual with a disability, you may request a reasonable accommodation during the job application and/or recruitment process. You can request reasonable accommodations by calling 212.846.5500 or by sending an email to paramountaccommodations@paramount.com. Only messages left for this purpose will be returned.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4458193015": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Overview\nWorking at Atlassian\nAtlassians can choose where they work – whether in an office, from home, or a combination of the two. That way, Atlassians have more control over supporting their family, personal goals, and other priorities. We can hire people in any country where we have a legal entity.\nTo help our teams work together effectively, this role is fully remote, but requires you to be located in either US Pacific or Mountain time zones .\nWe're looking for a Fullstack Software Engineer to join our team, passionately focused on delivering creative improvements for our engineering teams.\nResponsibilities\nWhat You'll Do:\nBuild REST APIs that power core customer experiences\nBuild customer-facing React components\nConfigure monitoring for backend services\nBuild CICD pipelines\nDevelop integrations with our content management system\nBuild features and services with reliability in mind\nCompensation\nAt Atlassian, we strive to design equitable, explainable, and competitive compensation programs. We follow consistent hiring practices and account for each candidate's skills, knowledge, and experience when setting base pay within the range.\nPlease visit go.atlassian.com/payzones for more information on which locations are included in each of our geographic pay zones. However, please confirm the zone for your specific location with your recruiter.\nThis role may also be eligible for benefits, bonuses, commissions, and equity.\nPay Ranges\nRole\nIn The United States , we have three geographic pay zones. For this role, our current base pay ranges for new hires in each zone are:\nZone A : $150,300 - $196,225\nZone B : $135,270 - $176,603\nZone C : $124,749 - $162,867\nQualifications\nYour Background:\n4+ years experience with JavaScript/TypeScript and supporting libraries (ex. ES6, React, Node)\nBachelor's or Master's degree with a preference for Computer Science degree\nExperience performing platform integrations using REST\nA background in working with GIT in a collaborative team setting\nFamiliarity writing cross-browser compliant HTML & Sass/CSS\nFamiliarity working with UX and Visual Designers\nFamiliarity with server technologies. (NPM, Docker, NGINX, Express/Node)\nA love for working collaboratively on a team with varied strengths\nIf You've Got These Skills, Even Better\nExperience working with an enterprise content management system\nExperience working with cloud platforms like AWS\nJava experience\nFreemarker experience\nRust experience\nBenefits & Perks\nAtlassian offers a wide range of perks and benefits designed to support you, your family and to help you engage with your local community. Our offerings include health and wellbeing resources, paid volunteer days, and so much more. To learn more, visit go.atlassian.com/perksandbenefits .\nAbout Atlassian\nAt Atlassian, we're motivated by a common goal: to unleash the potential of every team. Our software products help teams all over the planet and our solutions are designed for all types of work. Team collaboration through our tools makes what may be impossible alone, possible together.\nWe believe that the unique contributions of all Atlassians create our success. To ensure that our products and culture continue to incorporate everyone's perspectives and experience, we never discriminate based on race, religion, national origin, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, or marital, veteran, or disability status. All your information will be kept confidential according to EEO guidelines.\nTo provide you the best experience, we can support with accommodations or adjustments at any stage of the recruitment process. Simply inform our Recruitment team during your conversation with them.\nTo learn more about our culture and hiring process, visit go.atlassian.com/crh .\nIn line with local law, identity verification (which may include use of biometric data) is a condition of employment with Atlassian for employment fraud purposes.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4458795251": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "🌎 About Us\nAt TeamSnap, we believe when the world connects through sports; the world becomes better. TeamSnap is a sports and communication platform dedicated to taking the work out of play in youth sports. We also believe our jobs should excite us, our teammates should support us and our bosses should inspire us. We empower our people to bring big ideas and tiny egos, landing us on Outside Magazine’s list of “ Best Places to Work\" and Built In’s “ 100 Best Remote-First Places to Work.\"\nTeamSnap is seeking a Staff Software Engineer, Backend, to join our fully distributed engineering team and help us continue scaling systems that serve millions of daily users and tens of thousands of amateur sports organizations. Our primary backend stack includes Node and TypeScript, alongside Elixir, SQL, cloud-based services, event-driven systems, queues, background jobs, caching layers, and observability tooling.\nWe are looking for a hands-on Staff Backend Engineer with deep, meaningful production Node experience who can build and improve APIs and services, reason through production issues across the system, lead technical design in ambiguous areas, mentor engineers, and raise the quality bar across the team. This person should bring strong systems thinking that connects application architecture with infrastructure, platform, data, security, and other adjacent domains, bringing those teams into architecture and solutioning conversations early without being expected to own those functions directly.\nAs an engineering team, we architect and build scalable systems using service-oriented and event-driven architecture. This role will help shape the technical foundation behind TeamSnap’s product experience, with a focus on backend systems, APIs, services, data performance, reliability, observability, and production quality.\nWhat You'll Do:\nArchitect, build, and evolve backend APIs, services, event-driven workflows, queues, background jobs, data models, caching strategies, and integrations that support millions of users and thousands of sports organizations.\nOwn complex backend product and technical work from discovery through design, implementation, rollout, production support, and long term maintainability.\nLead ambiguous technical initiatives by breaking down problems, identifying risks, making practical tradeoffs, and helping teams move from uncertainty to clear execution.\nProvide technical leadership across our Node ecosystem by advancing shared patterns, standards, tooling, and practices, and helping engineers make better Node-specific architectural and operational decisions.\nConnect application architecture with platform, infrastructure, data, security, observability, and other adjacent domains, identifying concerns early and bringing the right teams into architecture, solutioning, and scaling decisions.\nImprove the reliability, scalability, performance, and operability of production systems through thoughtful architecture, strong testing practices, database optimization, caching, monitoring, alerting, and incident follow-up.\nDebug complex production issues by reasoning across application code, databases, caches, queues, jobs, observability data, and the broader request lifecycle.\nPartner with Product, Design, Engineering, Infrastructure, Platform, Data, Support, and other teams to turn roadmap needs into durable backend systems and practical delivery plans.\nStrong interpersonal skills with the ability to give and receive constructive feedback, mentor engineers, influence cross-team alignment and articulate technical trade-offs to non-technical stakeholders\nWhat Will Set You Up for Success:\nStaff level backend engineering depth, with deep, meaningful production Node experience at scale and a strong track record of architecting, building, operating, and improving complex backend systems.\nDeep Node and TypeScript experience, including strong understanding of runtime behavior, concurrency, failure modes, performance characteristics, production debugging, and the architectural tradeoffs involved in operating Node systems at scale.\nStrong systems thinking, with the ability to connect application architecture and runtime decisions with platform, infrastructure, data, security, observability, and other adjacent domains, bringing those perspectives and teams into the process early as systems are architected, built, and scaled.\nStrong SQL and relational database judgment, including indexing, query optimization, migrations, profiling, data modeling, transactions, read and write patterns, and performance tuning.\nPractical understanding of service-oriented architecture, event-driven architecture, queues, background jobs, webhooks, Redis or similar caching tools, and systems that need to scale under real production load.\nWorking knowledge of production infrastructure and platform concerns, enough to reason through deployments, containers, CI/CD pipelines, cloud services, networking basics, observability, and operational debugging.\nStrong production ownership mindset, with the ability to use logs, metrics, traces, dashboards, alerts, incident reviews, and system behavior to improve reliability over time.\nDemonstrated ability to lead through influence, mentor engineers, facilitate technical decisions, communicate tradeoffs clearly, and connect backend technical choices to customer impact, business needs, and long term maintainability.\nBonus:\nPrevious work in or close partnership with infrastructure, platform, SRE, DevOps, or data teams.\nElasticsearch experience, particularly operating, scaling, troubleshooting, or designing search and indexing workloads in production.\nFamiliarity with BigQuery, analytics pipelines, reporting workflows, or high-volume data processing.\nResponsible use of AI-assisted engineering workflows to improve debugging, testing, documentation, refactoring, prototyping, or developer experience without compromising quality or understanding.\nGot cold feet? If you’re thinking you don’t meet 100% of the above qualifications, you should still seriously consider applying . We’re all humans with special talents that go beyond what’s listed here.\nCompensation\nWe’re committed to equitable compensation for all TeamSnappers. The minimum starting point for this role is $200,000 inclusive of base and bonus, with comp updated based on multiple factors. Our comp is highly competitive in our space and we adjust overall comp based on relevant experience, skills, certifications, and geographic location.\n🖥 Location\nTeamSnap is a fully remote company, so you need to be very comfortable working with people who aren’t in the same time zone as you. We are always expanding, but there is a small list of states we do not hire in, including Alabama, Alaska, Delaware, District of Columbia, Hawaii, Iowa, Louisiana, Mississippi, Nebraska, New Mexico, Rhode Island, South Dakota West Virginia and Utah and while we love all parts of the world, we can only hire permanent US residents at this time.\n🚀 Opportunities to Grow\nAt TeamSnap, we work hard to provide a culture of trust, accountability, inclusivity, and boundless opportunities to grow, along with the chance to make a lasting impact and have some fun while doing it.\n🎩 Total Rewards\nWe're proud to be remote-first. We've been remote since 2009, long before COVID made it cool\nUnlimited PTO and paid parental leave for ALL parents (not just primary or secondary)\n100% premium coverage of medical/dental/vision for you and your family\n401K to help you invest for the future\n$1,500 annual learning and development stipend\nTravel to fun locations for all-company meetings and team events\nGenerous home office allowance to set you up for success\nTeamSnap SWAG to our store upon starting and a $50 credit on every work anniversary thereafter\nA monthly stipend reimbursement for health & wellness and so much more!\nTeamSnap Total Rewards\n🏆 Working at TeamSnap\nAt TeamSnap, you're not a culture fit, you're a culture add. Check out our Culture Playbook and learn how we succeed at being remote-first, what makes our company so unique, and how we're inspired by our people, our customers, and our values.\n🧡 Inclusion and Diversity\nCreativity and innovation can't thrive when we're cookie-cutter images of each other. We’re quickly growing more diverse, but there's always room for improvement. We are committed to inclusion and diversity at TeamSnap, and we hold ourselves accountable for building an environment where everyone feels valued. If you need any disability-related adaptation during the recruitment process, just let us know! We are an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer.\nWe may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of the hiring process, such as reviewing applications, analyzing resumes, or assessing responses and identifying potential inconsistencies or verification signals in application materials based on available information. These tools assist our recruitment team but do not replace human judgment. Final hiring decisions are ultimately made by humans. If you would like more information about how your data is processed, please contact us.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4470462790": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "SpinQuest is seeking a Staff Frontend Engineer - Mobile to join our team in the United States on a remote basis.\nWe are building a high growth social gaming platform with innovative currency mechanics, delivering fast, real time experiences across mobile and web. This role will primarily focus on building and scaling our mobile application from the ground up using React Native, with React and Next.js supporting our web platform.\nWhat You’ll Own\nDevelop scalable, high performance experiences for iOS and Android, including APIs, authentication, payments, and real time services\nArchitect and build production mobile applications from the ground up using React Native, owning the technical direction from initial architecture through launch.\nBuild reusable components, design systems, and frontend architecture that support rapid product growth and high traffic\nDevelop web experiences using React and Next.js while collaborating with product, design, backend, and creative teams\nIntegrate animations, interactive assets, and AI assisted workflows using tools such as Claude, Cursor, MCP, and structured Figma systems\nWhat We’re Looking For\n8+ years of senior level frontend engineering experience with proven experience building and launching React Native applications from the ground up\nStrong production experience with React Native, iOS and Android development, and scalable mobile architecture\nStrong proficiency with React and Next.js, including frontend architecture, state management, API integration, performance, and scalability\nExperience translating Figma designs and creative assets into polished production experiences, with a strong understanding of UX and visual quality\nExperience with AI assisted development tools such as Claude, Cursor, or MCP, with the ability to work autonomously in a fast paced startup environment\nBonus Points\nHistory of building production mobile applications from scratch using React Native, taking ownership from initial architecture through launch\nExperience launching applications through the Apple App Store or Google Play\nExperience with Figma MCP, design tokens, or AI assisted frontend workflows\nExperience with Rive, Lottie, animations, particle systems, or interactive UI\nBackground in gaming, iGaming, or other highly interactive consumer products\nExperience building automated asset pipelines, design systems, or reusable component libraries\n$190,000 - $220,000 a year\nAnnual performance bonus: 10% –15%\nBenefits & Total Rewards\nWe believe great talent deserves great benefits. SpinQuest offers comprehensive Health, Dental, and Vision coverage for employees, spouses, and dependents. SpinQuest covers 100% of employee health insurance premiums, offers a 4% 401(k) match. It’s a strong total rewards package designed to support you both today and as you grow with the company.\nAbout SpinQuest\nSpinQuest is a social casino platform built on a simple principle: made by players, for players. Founded in 2025, we've grown into one of the most recognized names in the social gaming space through deep partnerships with leading content creators, original in-house games, and a community-first approach to everything we build.\nOur brand extends well beyond the platform. We produce original content including documentary series and our own game show, develop collaborative game titles with creator partners, and host large-scale live events that bring our community together in person. Community investment is core to how we operate — including charitable activations that have returned more than $500,000 to local communities through toy drives, food drives, and community events.\nPlayers can enjoy casino-style games such as slots, blackjack, roulette, and craps purely for entertainment. Gameplay uses virtual coins that have no cash value, with free coins available daily and through ongoing promotions. Optional coin packages are available, but they are never required to enjoy the games. For more information, visit SpinQuest .\nWe may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of the hiring process, such as reviewing applications, analyzing resumes, or assessing responses and identifying potential inconsistencies or verification signals in application materials based on available information. These tools assist our recruitment team but do not replace human judgment. Final hiring decisions are ultimately made by humans. If you would like more information about how your data is processed, please contact us.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4480036512": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "CYBERR is the cybersecurity marketplace connecting virtual CISOs and security experts with startups and SMEs around the world. We’re looking for a curious, creative front-end developer who wants to build a great product and grow their knowledge of cybersecurity by working side by side with seasoned security leaders.\nMost front-end roles keep you in a bubble of UI tickets. At CYBERR, you’ll be surrounded by CISOs, security consultants, and compliance experts every day. You’ll see how real security missions are run, learn how attackers think, and understand what “secure by design” actually means in practice. If you’ve ever been curious about cybersecurity, this is the place to dive in.\nWhat you’ll do\nBuild and improve the CYBERR platform: client dashboards, expert profiles, mission matching, and booking flows\nTurn designs into fast, accessible, responsive interfaces\nCollaborate closely with product, back-end, and our community of cyber experts\nApply secure front-end practices (input validation, XSS and CSRF prevention, secure authentication flows) with guidance from security pros\nHelp shape the experience for both security experts and the startups who hire them\nWhat you’ll learn\nSecurity fundamentals from people who do it for a living\nSecure coding practices and how to spot vulnerabilities in your own code\nHow compliance frameworks like ISO 27001, SOC 2, and NIS2 shape real products\nHow to think like both a builder and a defender\nWho we’re looking for\nSolid experience with modern front-end development (React, Vue, or similar; TypeScript is a plus)\nA strong eye for UX, clean UI, and attention to detail\nComfort working in a fast-moving startup environment\nGenuine curiosity about cybersecurity (no prior security experience needed, just the desire to learn)\nGood communication skills in English; other languages are a bonus\nWhat we offer\nA front-row seat in the cybersecurity world, with mentorship from experienced security leaders\nReal ownership and impact on a growing international platform\nFlexible working arrangements [remote / hybrid / location]\nCompetitive compensation [details]\nA network of cyber professionals that can open doors for your whole career",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481015268": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Mercury's Design Systems team helps product teams build interfaces that feel consistent, accessible, and carefully considered. We're hiring a Frontend Engineer to help evolve the shared components and patterns behind those experiences, making it easier for teams across Mercury to turn good ideas into well-crafted software.\nYou'll work closely with designers and engineers to understand product needs, explore solutions, and carry improvements into the hands of the teams using them. This role is open to early-career and intermediate engineers. You'll build depth in frontend engineering and design systems through meaningful project ownership, with guidance from experienced teammates suited to your experience.\nDesign systems will be your initial focus within the team's broader Design Foundations work. As opportunities and interests align, you can also contribute to code-based prototyping and tools that help designers and AI agents work with Mercury's components. Strong AI fluency is part of how we build from the start.\nAs part of this role, you will:\nBuild shared components and patterns that make Mercury's interfaces better. You'll work in React and TypeScript, turning recurring product needs into flexible solutions that teams can use across different experiences.\nPartner with designers and product engineers to connect design intent with working software. Help evolve components and tokens across Figma and code, using feedback from real product work to improve the system.\nImprove the quality of the experiences built with our components. Consider how they look and behave for different users, bringing accessibility, thoughtful interactions, and reliable behavior into implementation and testing.\nMake the design system easier to use. Help teams adopt shared patterns and improve the examples, documentation, and workflows that let people build confidently with them.\nUse AI tools to explore approaches and move ideas into working code. Apply your judgment to what agents produce, test the results in context, and contribute useful approaches back to the team.\nWhat you'll bring:\nWe're interested in what you've built and how you think. Your experience may come from professional work, internships, coursework, open source, or personal projects.\nA foundation in React, TypeScript, HTML, and CSS, with experience building interfaces and the ability to explain the decisions behind your code.\nCare for visual craft and how people use software, including an interest in accessible interfaces and the details that make interactions feel right.\nHands-on fluency with AI coding tools. You can provide useful context, evaluate and improve generated code, and verify that it works as intended.\nOwnership and a willingness to learn: you follow work through, communicate when you need help, and use feedback to improve your approach.\nCuriosity about reusable systems and the tradeoffs involved in serving different product needs with shared components.\nAn interest in solving problems alongside designers and engineers, contributing ideas, and understanding the needs behind a request.\nExperience with design systems, prototyping, or developer tooling is a plus. You don't need to have held a design systems role to bring useful skills and ideas to this team.\nIf this role interests you, we invite you to explore our public demo at demo.mercury.com.\n*Mercury is a fintech company, not an FDIC-insured bank. Banking services provided through Choice Financial Group and Column N.A., Members FDIC.\nMercury values diversity & belonging and is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. All individuals seeking employment at Mercury are considered without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, or any other legally protected characteristic. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities or special needs. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.\nTotal Rewards\nThe total rewards package at Mercury includes base salary, equity (stock options/RSUs), and benefits.\nOur salary and equity ranges are highly competitive within the SaaS and fintech industry and are updated regularly using the most reliable compensation survey data for our industry. New hire offers are made based on a candidate’s experience, expertise, geographic location, and internal pay equity relative to peers.\nOur target new hire base salary ranges for this role are the following :\nUS employees (any location):\n$140,800—$158,400 USD\nCanadian employees (any location):\n$115,700—$149,700 CAD",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481445383": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "For our client, we are seeking a Software Engineer 4 - TV Product UI to join the team of a leader in the Hospitality & Recreation space.\nThis role will focus on building and refining consumer-facing television experiences that engage audiences and deliver seamless entertainment interactions. You will partner closely with product, design, and engineering teams to shape new features, improve usability, and translate business goals into intuitive UI solutions. The position calls for strong technical execution in a modern JavaScript/TypeScript stack, along with thoughtful decision-making to balance quality, complexity, and user impact.\nLocation: Remote\nCompensation: $250,000 – $413,000 annually\nResponsibilities\nBuild innovative UI features for the company's TV app\nCollaborate with product, design, and engineering teams to scope and develop user experiences\nWork with a TypeScript/JavaScript codebase using React and Redux for TV platforms\nEnsure feature quality by writing testable code and creating automation with test engineers\nMeasure the direct impact of your work on the business\nQualifications\n3+ years of experience with consumer-facing products or apps\nProficiency in JavaScript and TypeScript, with familiarity with Node.js and GraphQL\nInterest in user engagement and improving entertainment features\nAbility to bring unique perspectives and balanced views to team collaboration\nStrong judgment, independence, and a collaborative mindset when solving complex problems\nBenefits\nComprehensive health plans and mental health support\n401(k) retirement plan with employer match\nEquity-based compensation program\nDisability programs and health savings accounts\nFamily-forming benefits and life insurance\nGenerous paid time off policies, including 35 days for hourly employees and flexible time off for salaried employees\nOur client is an equal opportunity employer. We encourage you to apply even if you don’t meet every qualification—your background could be exactly what this team needs.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481809514": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Want to learn more about this role and Jobot? Click our Jobot logo and follow\nour LinkedIn page!\nJob details:\nTypeScript Developer | Own Full-Stack Architecture in a High-Impact Consulting Environment\nThis Jobot Job is hosted by: Andrew Nguyen\nAre you a fit? Easy Apply now by clicking the \"Easy Apply\" button\nand sending us your resume.\nSalary: $120,000 - $150,000 per year\nA bit about us:\nWe are a high-end technology consulting firm based in the Northern Virginia area. Our customers routinely call upon us to solve some of the largest scale and hardest problems in computer science and software development. If you have a solid grounding in software engineering, continuous delivery, and computer science, and are looking for a career opportunity to grow and leverage those skills to the fullest while working on cutting edge technologies – Here is the place to be!\nWhy join us?\n120-150k Base!\n15% Annual Bonuses!\nRemote Schedule!\n401K Matching!\nAccelerated Career Growth!\nChallenging Problems!\nJob Details\nWe are looking for a talented senior full-stack TypeScript software engineer with Devops chops who is passionate about technology to join our growing team of product, technology, and software professionals. The initial assignment for the new position is to develop a loan origination system for a financial services enterprise. The successful candidate will work with highly experienced team leads and have an opportunity to learn new technologies, while refining fundamental skills.\nJOB RESPONSIBILITIES\nDesign and build a loan origination system using Node, Apollo GraphQL, Angular, Camunda, and a suite of AWS components including but not limited to EKS, Lambda, S3, MSK, and Aurora. The components are primarily backend systems, but some frontend development will be needed.\nWork with tech leads and the product team to help determine functional requirements for the system.\nContribute as member of an Agile team and promote Agile practices\nProactively collaborate with our team on development and knowledge sharing\nQualifications\nSenior-level experience building GraphQL servers, including defining schemas, implementing resolvers, and producing GraphQL APIs.\nExperience implementing GraphQL federation or federated graph architectures across multiple services.\nStrong proficiency in TypeScript for backend or full-stack development.\nExperience consuming GraphQL APIs on the client side using tools such as Apollo Client or similar.\nExperience developing server-side applications with Node.js.\nHands-on experience deploying or supporting applications in AWS environments.\nExperience developing frontend applications using React or Angular.\nAbility to design and optimize GraphQL schemas and queries to ensure efficient data fetching between frontend and backend services.\nExperience collaborating across frontend and backend teams to support scalable GraphQL-based architectures.\nInterested in hearing more? Easy Apply now by clicking the \"Easy Apply\" button.\nJobot is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We provide an inclusive work environment that celebrates diversity and all qualified candidates receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, national origin, age (40 and over), disability, military status, genetic information or any other basis protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws. Jobot also prohibits harassment of applicants or employees based on any of these protected categories. It is Jobot’s policy to comply with all applicable federal, state and local laws respecting consideration of unemployment status in making hiring decisions.\nSometimes Jobot is required to perform background checks with your authorization. Jobot will consider qualified candidates with criminal histories in a manner consistent with any applicable federal, state, or local law regarding criminal backgrounds, including but not limited to the Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring and the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance.\nInformation collected and processed as part of your Jobot candidate profile, and any job applications, resumes, or other information you choose to submit is subject to Jobot's Privacy Policy, as well as the Jobot California Worker Privacy Notice and Jobot Notice Regarding Automated Employment Decision Tools which are available at jobot.com/legal.\nBy applying for this job, you agree to receive calls, AI-generated calls, text messages, or emails from Jobot, and/or its agents and contracted partners. Frequency varies for text messages. Message and data rates may apply. Carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages. You can reply STOP to cancel and HELP for help. You can access our privacy policy here: jobot.com/privacy-policy\nWant to learn more about this role\nand Jobot?\nClick our Jobot logo and follow our LinkedIn page!",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481891876": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This position offers a leadership role in designing and building scalable full stack systems, encompassing backend services, data models, and frontend architectures that support complex, data-driven product experiences. The candidate will operate as a hands-on technical leader, influencing core services and delivering end-to-end applications that leverage AI capabilities for enterprise insight and operational efficiency.\nKey Responsibilities\nLead the design, development, and deployment of full stack applications, including backend services, APIs (REST/GraphQL), and frontend interfaces, ensuring modularity, security, and high performance.\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams—Product, Design, Data Science—to translate requirements into intuitive, reliable user experiences and scalable backend solutions.\nDefine and evolve canonical data models, manage complex entity relationships (graphs, hierarchies), and develop indexing/search solutions (Elasticsearch, vector search) supporting AI-driven search and recommendation features.\nBuild event-driven architectures (Kafka, cloud pub/sub), implementing asynchronous workflows and stream processing for scalable, real-time data handling.\nIntegrate AI/ML functionalities—such as retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), semantic search, and entity resolution—into workflows, optimizing usability and business impact.\nEstablish frontend architecture using modern frameworks (React, Vue, Angular) with focus on performance, accessibility, and shared UI component libraries.\nDrive service reliability, system observability, automated testing, and continuous improvement practices.\nImplement robust security measures, including role-based (RBAC) and attribute-based access controls (ABAC), across all layers of the application stack.\nMentor engineering teams in architecture, code quality, and technical innovation, fostering best practices and engineering excellence.\nCoordinate with DevOps and Security to ensure compliant, scalable, and resilient infrastructure, primarily on cloud platforms like AWS.\nCore Qualifications & Requirements\n5+ years of professional full stack software engineering, with demonstrated leadership in complex enterprise systems.\nStrong expertise in backend frameworks (FastAPI, Django) and frontend frameworks (React, Vue, Angular) with modern build tools (Vite).\nProficiency in Python and TypeScript; solid understanding of data modeling (relational, NoSQL, graph databases).\nExtensive experience designing and consuming RESTful and GraphQL APIs, with large-scale, service-oriented architecture knowledge.\nHands-on experience with event-driven systems (Kafka, cloud pub/sub) and asynchronous processing pipelines.\nSkilled in implementing security controls (RBAC, ABAC) and multi-tenant applications, with familiarity in search technologies (Elasticsearch, vector search).\nDeep understanding of cloud-native development in AWS; CI/CD, observability, and automation practices.\nFamiliarity with AI/ML feature integration, including retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), semantic search, and AI workflow observability.\nAbility to translate technical solutions into scalable, business-oriented products and collaborate across multidisciplinary teams.\nNice-to-Have Qualifications\nAdvanced degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or related fields; relevant cloud certifications (AWS, Azure, GCP).\nExperience in data-intensive industries such as finance, property management, or enterprise analytics.\nActive use of AI coding assistants and agents, with an understanding of their application in modern software development workflows.\nKnowledge of search optimization and domain-specific data modeling within complex enterprise environments.\nCore Technical Skills\nBackend: Python, FastAPI, Django\nFrontend: React, Vue, Angular, Vite, JavaScript/TypeScript\nAPIs: REST, GraphQL\nDatabases: Relational (PostgreSQL, MySQL), NoSQL, Graph databases\nEvent systems: Kafka, cloud pub/sub (AWS SNS/SQS)\nSearch: Elasticsearch, vector search, retrieval systems\nCloud: AWS (S3, EC2, Lambda, CloudWatch)\nAI/ML: Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), semantic search, entity resolution, AI integrations\nSecurity: RBAC, ABAC, multi-tenancy\nDevOps: CI/CD pipelines, observability, automation\nCareer Impact\nJoin a forward-thinking organization driving innovation in knowledge automation through AI, where your leadership will directly influence the development of impactful enterprise solutions.\nCompensation and Benefits\n$200,000-$240,000, comprehensive benefits package, and flexible remote work options aligned with EST working hours. Occasional travel (2-3 times per year) is expected.\nApply Today!\nTake the next step in your career by contributing to a pioneering AI-driven platform with a dynamic team of industry leaders.\nThe Phoenix Group Advisors is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace and prohibit discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, or veteran status. We strive to attract talented individuals from all backgrounds and provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482466999": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Senior Full Stack Engineer\nLocation: Remote (US)\nAbout\nWe’re revolutionizing how B2B software companies build and manage integrations. As a leading embedded integration platform (iPaaS), we empower teams from startups to Fortune 100 enterprises to deliver seamless connectivity solutions. Recognized for top-tier customer satisfaction, our engineer-first platform combines a low-code visual builder with robust developer tools, enabling teams to focus on their core product while we handle the complexity of integrations.\nThe Role\nAs a Senior Full Stack Engineer , you’ll architect mission-critical features used by thousands of developers to build, deploy, and scale integrations. You’ll own projects end-to-end, from designing APIs to enhancing our low-code interface, directly impacting how businesses connect their software ecosystems.\nWhat You’ll Build\nIntegration Tools: Enhance our visual workflow builder and TypeScript SDK/CLI for developers\nScalable Infrastructure: Optimize systems handling millions of API calls and data transformations\nDeveloper Experiences: Improve dashboards, documentation, and APIs used by engineering teams globally\nCustomer Solutions: Troubleshoot complex integration scenarios with enterprise users\nTech Stack\nFrontend: TypeScript, React\nBackend: Python, Django, TypeScript\nCloud: AWS\nDatabases: Postgres, Redis\nKey Responsibilities\nLead architecture discussions and technical roadmapping for platform features\nShip production-grade code across the stack (frontend, backend, infrastructure)\nCollaborate with product and design to translate user needs into technical solutions\nMentor engineers and champion best practices (testing, code reviews, documentation)\nWork directly with customers to solve integration challenges\nWho We’re Looking For\n6+ years building production systems at scale, preferably in B2B SaaS\nTechnical Mastery:\nExpertise in TypeScript/React and Python/Django\nExperience designing GraphQL/REST APIs\nFamiliarity with cloud infrastructure (AWS) and relational databases\nMindset:\nThrives in collaborative, fast-paced environments\nObsessed with code quality and maintainability\nCommunicates complex technical concepts with clarity\nBonus Points For\nExperience building SDKs, CLIs, or developer tools\nBackground in integration platforms or iPaaS\nMentorship experience or open-source contributions\nWhy Join?\n🚀 Impact: Shape tools used by thousands to power critical business workflows\n💻 Tech Excellence: Work on cutting-edge problems in API orchestration and data pipelines\n💰 Compensation: base salary + equity\n🏡 Remote Flexibility: Work from anywhere in the US with biannual team gatherings\n🏥 Benefits:\nPremium medical/dental/vision (Cigna, Guardian, VSP)\n401(k) with 4% company match\nUnlimited PTO + life/disability insurance\nTop-tier hardware and tools\nOur Engineering Values\nBuild for Builders: Every feature is a developer experience\nShip to Learn: Iterate fast while maintaining enterprise-grade reliability\nCustomer-Centric Code: Solve real problems, not just write clever solutions\nApply Now if you:\nWant to redefine how software integrates at scale\nLove balancing technical depth with product intuition\nAre ready to mentor and lead in a high-growth environment\nWe review applications daily. Let’s connect!",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482694167": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "IMPORTANT: after you apply, please check your email. We send you a link to complete your application — it is not considered until that last step is done. If you do not see it, check your spam folder.\nThis is a fully remote position , open to candidates based in 55 countries, including United States, United Kingdom, Canada, Germany, India, France, Netherlands, Singapore.\nPay: $180,000–$250,000/yr\nJob Title: Software Engineer, New Grad\nJob Type: Full-time\nLocation : Remote\nThe Role\nThis is a fullstack software engineering role designed for recent graduates and early-career engineers looking to accelerate their growth by building production systems. You'll contribute to — and grow into owning — core internal platform capabilities and product features end-to-end.\nYou'll work across internal tools, services, workflows, and AI-powered products that support our engineering, operations, and recruiting platforms. As you grow, you'll take increasing ownership of critical systems while collaborating closely with experienced engineers.\nWhat You'll Own\nContribute to the design and development of end-to-end fullstack systems powering critical internal workflows and platform capabilities.\nBuild clean, maintainable backend services and APIs while learning scalable engineering best practices.\nDevelop high-quality frontend interfaces used by internal teams and end users.\nParticipate in data modeling and database optimization efforts, including schema design and query performance.\nCollaborate with product, operations, and design teams to translate ideas into reliable, production-ready features.\nImprove engineering quality through code reviews, testing, documentation, and continuous improvement.\nHelp troubleshoot production issues while learning how to build resilient, observable systems.\nDevelop sound engineering judgment by making thoughtful tradeoffs between speed, scalability, and maintainability.\nWhat We're Looking For\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Software Engineering, or a related field (recent graduate or graduating soon).\nInternship, co-op, research, or meaningful personal/project experience building software applications.\nStrong fundamentals in JavaScript and/or TypeScript.\nFamiliarity with frontend development using React or similar frameworks.\nFamiliarity with backend development using Node.js (NestJS is a plus).\nUnderstanding of relational databases such as PostgreSQL and core data modeling principles.\nFamiliarity with RESTful APIs and how distributed applications communicate.\nExposure to Git and modern software development workflows.\nStrong problem-solving skills, curiosity, attention to detail, and a growth mindset.\nExcited to learn quickly and contribute in a fast-moving engineering environment.\nPreferred\nInternship or professional software engineering experience.\nExposure to cloud platforms such as AWS, GCP, or Azure.\nFamiliarity with CI/CD, deployment pipelines, or DevOps fundamentals.\nExposure to modern architectures such as microservices, serverless, or event-driven systems.\nInterest in AI-powered products, workflow automation, or data-intensive applications.\nExperience contributing to team projects, hackathons, open-source software, or startup environments.\nCompensation & Benefits Notice\nThe national pay range for this full-time position is base salary of $110,000 –$150,000 USD. All employees are eligible for equity compensation, and employees may also receive performance-based bonuses, dependent on role and subject to company policies. The company provides a comprehensive benefits package, including up to 100% reimbursement for health-insurance premiums, paid time off, a 401(K) plan with a company match, and additional benefits designed to support a high-performing, remote-first workforce.\nthe company is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, or gender identity), national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable local laws, regulations and ordinances. If you need assistance and/or a reasonable accommodation during the application process, reach out to us by replying to our email.\nOur hiring process utilizes artificial intelligence tools to assist in candidate screening and assessment. Our AI tools are designed to complement, not replace, human decision-making.\nDisclaimer\nThe information contained in this job posting, including but not limited to role responsibilities, qualifications, compensation, and benefits, is provided for informational purposes only and does not constitute a binding offer of employment. the company reserves the right to amend, modify, or withdraw any portion of this posting at its sole discretion and without prior notice. All employment decisions are made in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.\nHow To Apply\nApply here with your profile. We will then email you a link to complete your application on the hiring platform — your application is only considered once that final step is done.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482932734": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This position is listed on behalf of a partner company, which manages all applications and next steps. Our partner is looking for an Associate Software Engineer based in the United States.\nWe are seeking a motivated Associate Software Engineer to contribute to the development, testing, and continuous improvement of innovative software solutions in the healthcare technology sector. In this role, you will collaborate with experienced engineers and cross-functional teams to build reliable, scalable, and maintainable applications that support better healthcare outcomes. You will work with modern development practices and AI-assisted engineering tools to streamline workflows, improve code quality, and accelerate software delivery. The position also offers opportunities to explore data platforms, machine learning pipelines, and generative AI technologies while strengthening your technical expertise. You will contribute to architectural discussions, quality assurance, documentation, and reusable engineering practices within a collaborative and supportive environment. This is an excellent opportunity for an early-career engineer eager to grow professionally while making a meaningful impact through technology.\nAccountabilities\nSoftware Development: Collaborate with engineering teams to design, develop, test, and maintain software applications. Write clean, efficient, secure, and maintainable code that follows established development standards and best practices.\nFeature Development and Enhancement: Contribute to the implementation of new features, application improvements, and technical solutions aligned with business and project requirements.\nCode Reviews and Quality Assurance: Participate in peer code reviews, identify potential improvements, and help ensure code quality, consistency, reliability, and compliance with engineering standards.\nTroubleshooting and Debugging: Investigate software defects, diagnose technical issues, implement corrective solutions, and support ongoing application maintenance.\nTesting and Validation: Develop and execute tests to validate application functionality, reliability, and performance, ensuring solutions meet defined quality requirements.\nCross-Functional Collaboration: Work closely with engineers and other stakeholders to understand requirements, clarify technical specifications, and deliver effective software solutions.\nAI-Assisted Engineering: Apply AI-powered development tools throughout the software delivery lifecycle, including requirements analysis, coding, testing, debugging, documentation, and operational monitoring.\nArchitecture and Solution Design: Use AI-assisted workflows to explore design alternatives, evaluate architectural approaches, improve existing systems, and prepare technical design artifacts for review.\nAI Output Validation: Assess AI-generated code and other technical outputs for correctness, security, maintainability, regulatory compliance, and alignment with business needs. Help review AI-assisted work produced by other engineers.\nData Platform Development: Contribute to the design and maintenance of data platforms and governed datasets that support analytics, machine learning, and generative AI applications.\nReusable Engineering Practices: Develop and share reusable prompts, AI agents, engineering playbooks, development workflows, and automation patterns that improve productivity across the engineering organization.\nDocumentation and Continuous Improvement: Maintain clear technical documentation, stay informed about emerging technologies, and recommend improvements to engineering tools, processes, and delivery practices.\nResponsible AI and Compliance: Ensure that AI-assisted development activities follow organizational policies and applicable requirements for intellectual property, information security, privacy, protected health information (PHI), and responsible AI use.\nRequirements\nEducation: Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical discipline.\nProgramming Skills: Proficiency in at least one programming language, such as C# or Python, with the ability to write readable, efficient, and maintainable code.\nSoftware Development Fundamentals: Basic understanding of software engineering principles, application development lifecycles, testing methodologies, debugging techniques, and coding best practices.\nVersion Control: Familiarity with Git or comparable version control systems for managing code changes and collaborating with other developers.\nAgile Methodologies: Understanding of software development methodologies such as Agile and Scrum, including collaborative planning, iterative delivery, and continuous improvement.\nProblem-Solving Skills: Strong analytical thinking, attention to detail, and the ability to investigate technical issues and develop practical solutions.\nCommunication and Collaboration: Good written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to work effectively within a team, receive feedback, and contribute to shared engineering objectives.\nAdaptability and Learning: Willingness to learn new technologies, explore emerging engineering practices, and continuously improve technical capabilities.\nAI-Assisted Development Experience: Familiarity with AI-powered coding tools and a demonstrated ability to use them effectively in software development is preferred. Relevant platforms may include GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Claude Code, or similar solutions.\nPrompt Engineering and AI Delivery: Strong prompt-writing skills and experience applying AI-assisted techniques to coding, testing, debugging, and other stages of software delivery are desirable.\nData and AI Technologies: Exposure to machine learning data pipelines, vector search, document processing, data preparation, or generative AI workloads is an advantage.\nData Governance: Working knowledge of data governance, data lineage, data quality, and observability practices supporting reliable AI-enabled solutions is preferred.\nSecurity and Responsible AI: Understanding of secure software development, privacy protection, intellectual property safeguards, and responsible AI principles, particularly in environments handling sensitive healthcare information.\nRemote Work Readiness: Ability to work remotely with a reliable high-speed internet connection exceeding 10 Mbps and the technical setup required to perform the role effectively.\nBenefits\nComprehensive Benefits Package: Access to a range of employee benefits, including health insurance, for eligible employees.\nRemote Work Environment: Work-from-home flexibility designed to support productivity and work-life balance.\nWork-Life Balance: A workplace culture that values employee wellbeing, flexibility, and autonomy.\nProfessional Development: Opportunities to expand technical skills, learn emerging technologies, and develop expertise in software engineering and AI-assisted development.\nInnovative Technology Exposure: Hands-on experience with AI-powered engineering tools, machine learning data platforms, and generative AI development practices.\nCollaborative Culture: Opportunities to work alongside engineers and cross-functional colleagues in an environment that values inclusion, teamwork, and continuous learning.\nMeaningful Impact: The opportunity to contribute to technology solutions that support healthcare organizations and help improve outcomes for people with complex medical needs.\nInclusive Workplace: A commitment to equal employment opportunities, accessibility, and respect for diverse backgrounds and perspectives.\nCompensation: Salary details were not specified in the available job posting. Compensation is determined according to the position's requirements, the selected candidate's skills, and relevant professional experience.\nHow Jobgether Works\nWe use an AI-powered matching process to ensure your application is reviewed quickly, objectively, and fairly against the role's core requirements. Our system identifies the top-fitting candidates, and this shortlist is then shared directly with the hiring company. The final decision and next steps (interviews, assessments) are managed by their internal team.\nWe appreciate your interest and wish you the best!\nWhy Apply Through Jobgether?\nData Privacy Notice: By submitting your application, you acknowledge that Jobgether will process your personal data to evaluate your candidacy and share relevant information with the hiring employer. This processing is based on legitimate interest and pre-contractual measures under applicable data protection laws (including GDPR). You may exercise your rights (access, rectification, erasure, objection) at any time.\nWe may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of the hiring process, such as reviewing applications, analyzing resumes, or assessing responses and identifying potential inconsistencies or verification signals in application materials based on available information. These tools assist our recruitment team but do not replace human judgment. Final hiring decisions are ultimately made by humans. If you would like more information about how your data is processed, please contact us.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483422876": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "AI Automation & Full-Stack Product Engineer\nWhat if AI could do more than just write a caption?\nCould it help launch and optimise ads?\nBuild landing pages?\nTurn an idea into copy, static creatives and scripts?\nGenerate UGC-style content?\nAutomate reporting?\nAnswer internal questions?\nHandle repetitive client communication?\nHelp our team make better decisions faster?\nThat’s what we want to find out and build.\nCerealBox is looking for its first in-house AI Automation & Full-Stack Product Engineer : someone who can take a real business problem, figure out the smartest technical solution, build it, launch it, maintain it and continuously improve it as better AI models and tools become available.\nThis isn’t a role where someone gives you a list of tickets every morning.\nYou’ll be expected to ask:\n“Why are we doing this manually?”\n“Can AI solve this?”\n“Should we build it ourselves or integrate an existing tool?”\n“How do we make this 10x better?”\nAnd then actually make it happen. 🚀\nA little about CerealBox\nWe’re a UK-based creative and performance agency working exclusively with charities.\nWe manage digital fundraising and paid media for around 30 charity clients and have already built our own analytics platform, True ROAS , to connect advertising spend with actual donation revenue.\nNow we want to take the next step.\nWe want AI and automation embedded across the business not because it sounds cool, but because it can genuinely help our team work smarter, move faster and deliver better results for charities.\nYour first big responsibility\nYou’ll take ownership of True ROAS , our existing production platform used by our media buyers, creative team and leadership.\nToday, it already handles:\nAttribution between Meta Ads and donation data\nROAS reporting by client, campaign and creative\nThousands of creatives and performance insights\nCommercial and settlement reporting\nScheduled data syncs and API integrations\nCurrency conversion and system monitoring\nYou’ll maintain it, improve it and help decide what it becomes next.\nThen comes the fun part 🤖\nSome of the problems we want you to explore include:\nAI Copywriting: Can AI consistently produce strong advertising copy?\nCreative Generation: Can static ad concepts and designs be automated?\nScript Writing: Can AI develop better hooks, concepts and video scripts?\nUGC: How much of UGC production can be generated using AI?\nVideo Editing: Can AI take raw footage and produce high-quality finished ads?\nMedia Buying: Can an AI agent help launch, monitor and optimise campaigns?\nCreative Ideation: Can AI generate genuinely interesting campaign concepts rather than generic ideas?\nLanding Pages: Can we rapidly generate and optimise fundraising landing pages?\nReporting: Can reporting become almost completely automated?\nInternal AI Assistant: Can we make tools like Toast smarter so our team can simply ask questions and get useful answers?\nClient Communication: Can AI safely respond to common or repetitive queries?\nWorkflow Automation: Can we remove repetitive operational work across the company?\nMeta + LLM Integrations: How can Meta data interact with models such as Claude and other LLMs?\nYou won't necessarily build every idea exactly as described.\nPart of your job is deciding what is actually worth building.\nWhat you’ll do\n🧠 AI & Automation\nIdentify repetitive work that can be automated\nResearch AI tools, APIs, models and agents\nPrototype solutions quickly\nDecide whether we should build, integrate or buy\nTurn successful experiments into reliable production tools\nKeep our AI systems current as models and technologies evolve\n💻 Full-Stack Engineering\nBuild and maintain modern React and TypeScript applications\nOwn backend architecture, APIs and database logic\nWork extensively with PostgreSQL and Supabase\nBuild reliable third-party integrations\nMaintain scheduled jobs and data pipelines\nMonitor failures and make sure systems are reliable and secure\n🎨 Product & UX\nSpeak directly with the people using your tools\nUnderstand the actual problem before writing code\nDesign simple, useful interfaces\nTake features from rough idea → prototype → production\nMeasure whether people actually use what you build\nImprove products based on real feedback\nOur current stack\nFrontend\nReact • Vite • TypeScript • TanStack Router & Query • Tailwind • shadcn/ui\nBackend & Data\nSupabase • PostgreSQL • Edge Functions • pg_cron • Row-Level Security\nHosting\nVercel\nIntegrations\nMeta Marketing API • Fundraising platform APIs • AI/LLM APIs\nWays of working\nGitHub • Pull Requests • AI-assisted development\nAnd yes if you can show us that part of the stack should change, we’re open to the conversation.\nWe’d love to speak to you if you have\n4+ years of professional software engineering experience\nStrong full-stack experience with React and TypeScript\nSolid PostgreSQL, data modelling and API experience\nExperience owning production systems\nExperience integrating third-party APIs\nStrong product thinking — not just coding from specifications\nThe ability to design clean interfaces without waiting for perfect Figma files\nConfidence working independently and making technical decisions\nCuriosity around AI, automation, agents and LLM APIs\nClear communication with non-technical teammates\nEven better if you’ve worked with\nSupabase\nMeta Marketing API\nPerformance marketing or ad-tech\nMarketing analytics\nClaude, OpenAI or other LLM APIs\nAI agents / tool calling / MCP\nData visualisation\nCharity or fundraising technology\nEarly-stage products or agencies\nYou do not need to tick every single box.\nIf you’ve built real products, love figuring things out and can show us interesting things you’ve shipped, we’d still like to hear from you.\nWhat you’ll get\n✨ A genuinely high-ownership role\n🤖 The freedom to experiment with AI and emerging technology\n🚀 The opportunity to build products that are actually used every day\n🌍 Exposure to an international UK-based agency environment\n💡 Direct access to leadership and the people using what you build\n📚 Space to research, test and introduce better technology\n🏖️ 21 days paid annual leave\n❤️ Work that ultimately helps charities raise more money\nWhat success looks like\nWe don’t simply want a longer codebase.\nWe want:\nless repetitive work, better data, smarter tools, faster decisions and AI systems that genuinely make the CerealBox team better at what it does.\nIf reading this already has you thinking, “I know how I’d build that…” we should probably talk. 👀\n📩 Apply with your CV, LinkedIn/GitHub profile and, most importantly, examples of products, automations or AI-powered tools you’ve actually built.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483527878": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Objective\nYour role as Software Engineer is to independently design, develop, test, and maintain full-stack software solutions across backend and frontend layers. You will own assigned features from requirement analysis through implementation, integration, QA handover, and production support, while ensuring solutions are reliable, maintainable, secure, and aligned with established engineering standards.\nMain Tasks\nDesign, develop, and maintain backend services, APIs, business logic, data processing, frontend applications, dashboards, portals, forms, reporting screens, internal tools, and reusable components.\nOwn assigned features from requirement analysis through development, testing support, QA handover, defect resolution, and production support, with limited supervision.\nImplement complete end-to-end features covering frontend user interactions, backend processing, PostgreSQL data persistence, event queue processing, integrations, and final user or system responses.\nDesign and consume REST APIs, including request and response models, validations, authentication, authorization, error handling, and appropriate integration behavior.\nImplement and maintain integration flows with internal services, operators, aggregators, third-party systems, callbacks, and webhooks, ensuring proper error handling and operational visibility.\nDevelop and validate PostgreSQL queries and database interactions, including transaction behavior, indexing, constraints, data persistence, and consistency requirements for assigned features.\nImplement and support RabbitMQ and event-driven workflows, including event publishing, message consumption, payload validation, retries, dead-letter handling awareness, logging, and queue-processing monitoring.\nImplement and support asynchronous workflows such as notifications, billing triggers, delivery reports, background jobs, audit events, and integration callbacks according to system requirements.\nAnalyze business and technical requirements, identify implementation gaps and dependencies, and propose appropriate technical approaches for assigned features before development.\nTroubleshoot and resolve technical issues across backend services, APIs, frontend behavior, PostgreSQL results, event queues, integrations, asynchronous processes, and end-to-end application flows.\nPerform unit testing, support integration and regression testing, resolve identified defects, and validate implemented changes before QA handover and release.\nOptimize standard application performance, including API response times, frontend rendering behavior, PostgreSQL queries, database interactions, and event-processing efficiency.\nCollaborate with QA, Product, DevOps, Support, Security, and other engineering teams to resolve dependencies and ensure smooth end-to-end delivery.\nProvide basic technical guidance to Junior Software Engineers when required and support them in resolving straightforward development and troubleshooting issues.\nEscalate complex architectural, scalability, security, performance, event-driven design, and production-critical concerns to Senior or Lead Software Engineers when required.\nMaintain technical documentation covering APIs, integrations, frontend components, database interactions, event flows, application workflows, configurations, and known technical limitations.\nEnsure development activities comply with Jira traceability, Git and branching practices, pull request and code review requirements, SonarQube validation, secure coding, documentation, and release standards.\nQualifications\nBachelor’s degree in computer science, Software Engineering, Computer Engineering, Information Technology, or a related field.\n2+ years of experience in software development across backend and frontend applications.\nHands-on experience developing and integrating APIs, databases, and full-stack application features.\nExperience with database-driven applications, event-driven or asynchronous processing, and system integrations.\nExposure to messaging, real-time, high-volume, or integration-heavy platforms is considered an advantage.\nProfessional proficiency in Local Language and English is required.\nGood hands-on knowledge of backend development using Java or C#.NET and frontend development using React and Next.js.\nGood understanding of REST APIs, authentication, authorization, integration patterns, callbacks, webhooks, and error handling.\nGood knowledge of PostgreSQL, SQL queries, transactions, indexing fundamentals, constraints, data persistence, and validation.\nGood understanding of RabbitMQ or similar event-queuing technologies, including producers, consumers, message handling, retries, dead-letter concepts, and asynchronous processing.\nAbility to independently develop and troubleshoot complete features across backend, frontend, database, integration, and event-processing layers.\nGood knowledge of Git workflows, branching strategies, pull requests, code reviews, and development traceability.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483638039": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "5. Lumicera\nFrontend Developer\n$130 K\nfully Remote\nA frontend-focused engineer responsible for developing modern, responsive, maintainable user interfaces for enterprise healthcare and pharmacy applications. This individual should be very strong in React and comfortable integrating frontend applications with .NET-based backend services.\nMust-have technical skills\nStrong hands-on React development.\nJavaScript and TypeScript.\nReact Hooks, functional components, and state management.\nREST API integration and handling asynchronous data.\nHTML, CSS, responsive layouts, and reusable components.\nFrontend debugging, performance optimization, and testing.\nAbility to work independently on complex user interfaces.\nPreferred: Redux or Context API, React Testing Library, Jest, CI/CD, healthcare applications, and basic C#/.NET knowledge.",
