          "description": "About the job\nMeeBoss is sharing this active opportunity on behalf of Voltus, a leading company for Distributed Energy Resources (DERs) that aims to be the platform fulfilling the promise of the energy transition.\nThis role is appropriate for entry-level to early-career engineering candidates eager to build scalable software for Voltus.\nYou will join a fully remote team tackling complex energy industry challenges, collaborating with experienced engineers on a modern tech stack, and contributing to core systems that decarbonize the grid.\nJob title\nSoftware Engineer\nCompany\nMeeBoss\nLocation\nRemote\nCompensation\nBase pay is $110,000-$140,000 USD annually, commensurate with experience, with a 10% annual bonus and equity.\nWhy this role\nJoin a fully remote team distributed across the US, Canada, and abroad.\nContribute to core systems that decarbonize the grid and provide flexibility, reliability, and resilience to the energy market.\nCollaborate with experienced engineers on a modern tech stack including Python, Postgres, Go, FastAPI, and React.\nWhat you will do\nWrite clean, maintainable, and well-tested code to support the team’s projects.\nContribute to the design and implementation of new features and services.\nCollaborate with your team to troubleshoot and resolve issues in the production environment.\nParticipate in code reviews to learn from and contribute to the team’s shared knowledge.\nWork with stakeholders to understand requirements and translate them into technical solutions.\nWhat we are looking for\nA Bachelor’s degree, or equivalent combination of education and experience, in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical field.\nFoundational programming skills in a backend language like Python.\nA strong desire to learn and grow as a software engineer.\nExcellent communication and collaboration skills.\nA genuine passion for creating a cleaner, more resilient energy future.\nAuthorization to work in the US or Canada without sponsorship.\nA link to your GitHub account in the application (applications without a GitHub account will not be considered).\nBenefits\nUnlimited PTO for full-time employees.\nParental leave.\nComprehensive benefits package to promote health, wellness, and financial security.\nAbout MeeBoss\nMeeBoss helps job seekers and hiring teams make direct, relevant career connections.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484752899": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Join Boeing and help develop software that supports critical defense missions. This entry-level opportunity is based in Maryland Heights, Missouri, and offers the chance to contribute to next-generation mission planning technology while building your software engineering career.\nAbout The Company\nAt Boeing, we innovate and collaborate to make the world a better place. We are committed to creating a welcoming, respectful, and inclusive environment where teammates can grow and contribute. Tapestry Solutions, a Boeing company and part of Boeing Global Services, brings more than 30 years of experience designing, implementing, training, and supporting information technology and business intelligence solutions. Its approximately 500 professionals serve 75 defense, commercial, and government clients across more than 50 U.S. locations and nine countries.\nTapestry Solutions combines Boeing’s resources with the agility and people-focused culture of a smaller business. Employees take ownership, pursue excellence, and develop innovative solutions that support important missions and the safety of customers and colleagues around the world.\nAbout The Role\nBoeing is seeking an Entry-Level Software Engineer to join a team developing and maintaining weapon planning software for the U.S. Air Force. You will contribute to the next-generation Mission Planning system for the Department of Defense as part of a software development scrum team. The team follows the Scaled Agile Framework (SAFe) and uses a microservices architecture, with TypeScript and React for front-end development and primarily C# for back-end services.\nThis is a first-shift, U.S.-based position. Applicants must meet applicable U.S. export-control requirements, and the role requires the ability to obtain a U.S. Secret security clearance. U.S. citizenship is required to obtain the government clearance. Boeing does not provide employment visa sponsorship, and relocation assistance is not available for this position.\nQualifications\nRequired qualifications include a bachelor’s degree or higher, experience with C#, and the ability to obtain a U.S. Secret clearance. Candidates must also meet U.S. export-control requirements as a U.S. Person, as defined by applicable regulations. This includes U.S. citizens, U.S. nationals, lawful permanent residents, refugees, and asylees.\nPreferred candidates may have a bachelor’s degree in engineering, engineering technology, chemistry, physics, mathematics, data science, or computer science, along with relevant experience. Equivalent combinations of education and experience may also be considered, including a bachelor’s degree with four or more years of directly related experience, or eight or more years of relevant experience. Additional desired qualifications include familiarity with Agile or Scrum, JavaScript or TypeScript, relational databases, at least one year of full software development life-cycle experience, and AWS, C2S, or other cloud environments.\nResponsibilities\nWith general supervision, develop, document, maintain, and unit-test software using development environments and languages such as C#, TypeScript, JavaScript, and React. Apply established methods and practices to software design and help specify and maintain software requirements. Investigate defects, troubleshoot operational and integration issues, gather supporting information, and collaborate with teammates to recommend solutions.\nYou will also integrate and compile software components into builds, test component-level software in the target environment, document deployed processes and tools, and collect relevant metrics. The position may include other duties as assigned.\nBenefits\nBoeing offers a competitive total rewards package designed to attract, engage, and retain talented employees. Depending on eligibility, benefits may include health insurance, flexible spending accounts, health savings accounts, retirement savings plans, life and disability insurance, and paid and unpaid time away from work. Available programs may vary based on factors such as location and date of hire.\nThe expected base pay range is $65,000–$72,680. Actual compensation depends on candidate experience and qualifications, as well as market and business considerations. Eligible employees may also have access to variable compensation opportunities. This is a drug-free workplace; post-offer applicants and employees may be subject to testing under company policy when applicable. Applications are expected to be accepted through November 7, 2026.\nEqual Opportunity\nBoeing is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, physical or mental disability, genetic factors, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484759397": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "What You’ll Be Doing\nCadmus is seeking a Junior Full Stack Developer to join our Federal Operations Group. This role provides full-stack software development support to a file management application team, a high-performing Agile team responsible for delivering enterprise platforms and shared services that support multiple systems at a federal government health care organization. This solution includes file management activities including uploading and downloading files for a major federal healthcare organization. Other functionalities include large file transfers, file workflows, anti-virus scanning, PHI/PII scanning and other capabilities related to the secure transfer of files. It is anticipated that this file management application will undergo a complete redesign in the next few months.\nWho We Are\nCadmus provides government, commercial, and other private organizations worldwide with technology-empowered advisory and implementation services. We help our clients achieve their goals and drive lasting, impactful change by leveraging transformative digital solutions and unparalleled expertise across domains.\nAt Cadmus, we look for team players and problem solvers who are driven to use their unique perspectives and intellectual curiosity to help deliver breakthrough solutions that achieve transformative goals. As a member of our team, you'll collaborate with leading experts to support our clients across the globe. We offer competitive compensation, outstanding health care and retirement benefits, a vibrant and collaborative work environment, and ample opportunities for professional growth.\nJoin Cadmus. Together, we are strengthening society and the natural world. For more information, visit cadmusgroup.com .\nResponsibilities\n1–2 years of hands-on experience building and maintaining web applications using modern frontend and backend technologies.\nCollaborate with senior developers, product owners, and DevOps engineers to design, develop, test, and deploy scalable applications on cloud infrastructure.\nDevelop responsive and interactive user interfaces using Angular and /or React.\nDesign, develop, and maintain backend services using Python and/or JavaScript (NodeJS).\nDesign, implement, and integrate REST APIs with frontend applications and third-party services.\nDeploy, configure, and maintain applications on AWS cloud services.\nWork in Linux environments for application deployment, troubleshooting, and automation.]\nWrite clean, maintainable, and well-documented code following coding standards.\nParticipate in code reviews, debugging, testing, and performance optimization.\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams using Agile/Scrum methodologies.\nTroubleshoot production issues and assist in maintaining application availability.\nQualifications\nBachelor’s degree in computer science, Information Technology, or a related field (or equivalent practical experience).\n1–2 years of experience in full stack web development - Python, JavaScript, NodeJS\nExperience with relational databases (PostgreSQL, MySQL, or similar).\nProficiency with Git and collaborative development workflows.\nFamiliarity with CI/CD pipelines (Jenkins CJE) and DevOps practices.\nExperience with Docker and Kubernetes.\nKnowledge of HTML5, CSS3, and JavaScript/TypeScript.\nKnowledge of automated testing frameworks and test-driven development.\nComfortable in stepping out of the comfort zone to suggest, test, implement new technologies and frameworks.\nAbility to independently research and suggest solutions for ongoing improvement including new frameworks and infrastructure requirements.\nA passion for scaling software, ensuring high availability enjoyment of automation and demonstrate a proactive approach to detecting and resolving issues.\nMust be a self-starter\nStrong communication skills - both written and verbal. The ability to articulate ideas to non-technical audience.\nAgile oriented in approach to engineering and operations, including being comfortable with ambiguity in a flat organization.\nBelieve in a quick improvement approach: Fail fast, learn fast, improve fast.\nAbility to obtain a Public Trust is required.\nPreferred Skills\nAdded project-relevant areas such as S3, ECS/Fargate, SQS, EventBridge, API Gateway, IAM, KMS, RBAC, secure APIs, and file-processing security.\nExperience with Infrastructure as Code (Terraform or CloudFormation).\nFamiliarity with messaging systems such as Kafka, or Amazon SQS.\nExperience implementing authentication and authorization (OAuth2, JWT, SAML).\nFamiliarity with monitoring and logging tools.\nKnowledge of security best-practices for web applications.\nExperience working in a DevOps-oriented environment.\nConfigure and manage Nginx as a web server and reverse proxy or has experience with similar technologies like Tomcat, Apache.\nFamiliarity with AI Assisted coding practices/tools (Co-Pilot, Cursor etc.).\nAdditional Information\nCandidates must be eligible to work in the United States as a U.S Perm Resident or U.S. Citizen.\nBased on eligibility and job status, Cadmus offers an excellent benefits package to include: medical, dental, vision, company paid disability and life insurance, 401(k) program, paid time off (PTO), paid holidays, voluntary time off (VTO), tuition reimbursement, adoption assistance program, other optional benefits and various bonus programs.\nThe salary range for this position is $80,000 - $100,000. The actual salary will be determined by several factors, including relevant work experience, education, skills, and market competitiveness.\nWe value the critical role safety and health protocols contribute to everyone’s success at Cadmus, and work together to align and comply with all federal, state, and local safety and health mandates to ensure a safe and valuable work environment.\nCadmus is an Equal Opportunity Employer and prohibits unlawful discrimination. Cadmus is committed to providing a respectful workplace where equal employment opportunities are available to all applicants and employees without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation (including gender identity and/or expression), national origin, military and veteran status, physical and mental disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\nLearn more about Cadmus by visiting our website at: cadmusgroup.com .",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
