        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About the Job\nStartupSphere is seeking a Node.js Developer to design, develop, test, and deliver software applications that serve a large user base. This role emphasizes software quality, automated testing, release coordination, and end-to-end project ownership.\nThe ideal candidate will have at least one year of relevant experience, a solid understanding of software development best practices, and the ability to collaborate with quality assurance teams, stakeholders, and remote colleagues. The position offers an opportunity to take ownership of technical projects and contribute to software improvements in a remote-first environment.\nAbout the Company\nStartupSphere is described in the listing as an Anchorage, Alaska-based company transitioning toward a remote-native working model. The company emphasizes individual ownership, problem-solving, collaboration, and opportunities for professional development.\nKey Responsibilities\nCollaborate with quality assurance teams to define test coverage and identify regressions early.\nMaintain code quality through automated linting, testing, and static analysis.\nIdentify and resolve software defects during staging and testing.\nAnalyze existing technical patterns and recommend cleaner, more maintainable solutions.\nCoordinate software releases with stakeholders and distributed teams.\nDevelop Terraform integration tests to identify regressions before deployment.\nSupport application and infrastructure migration activities according to project deadlines.\nTake ownership of technical issues and implement improvements with minimal supervision.\nFollow established technology best practices and industry standards.\nWork collaboratively with remote teams to deliver reliable software.\nRequired Qualifications and Skills\nAt least 1 year of relevant professional experience.\nUnderstanding of software development principles and industry best practices.\nFamiliarity with automated testing, linting, and static analysis.\nAbility to recognize software defects and troubleshoot technical issues.\nStrong analytical and pattern-recognition skills.\nEffective communication and the ability to explain technical findings clearly.\nAbility to coordinate work with QA teams, stakeholders, and remote colleagues.\nA proactive approach to problem-solving and project ownership.\nTechnical Skills\nBackend Development: Node.js development experience.\nSoftware Quality: Automated testing, linting, and static analysis.\nInfrastructure Testing: Terraform integration testing.\nApplication Maintenance: Debugging, regression prevention, and code quality improvements.\nMigration Support: Familiarity with application or infrastructure migration activities.\nThe original listing also references a Laravel technology stack, but it does not provide detailed technical requirements or clarify how Laravel relates to the Node.js role.\nCompensation and Benefits\nAnnual Salary: $76,000–$109,000 USD.\nBenefits: The company advertises a benefits package, but specific benefits are not detailed in the supplied listing.\nProfessional Development: Opportunities to build technical skills and take ownership of projects.\nWork Schedule and Location\nJob Title: Node.js Developer\nCompany Listed: Energy Innovation Corp\nOrganization Described: StartupSphere\nLocation: Anchorage, Alaska, United States\nWork Arrangement: Remote\nExperience Level: Entry-level to early-career\nRequired Experience: At least 1 year\nImportant Listing Notes\nThe supplied listing contains inconsistencies: Energy Innovation Corp appears as the employer in the job header, while StartupSphere is identified as the hiring company in the description. Some listed responsibilities also refer to Anchorage-specific deployments, Laravel, Terraform, and interpersonal skills without clearly explaining their connection to the Node.js position.\nCandidates should verify the actual employer, core technology stack, responsibilities, and remote-work arrangements before applying.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484970716": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:27:57.470191+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Company\nSynergisticIT works with organizations seeking technology talent and supports professionals as they build skills for careers in the IT industry. The company focuses on connecting qualified candidates with opportunities in areas such as software development, data, cloud computing, and related technology disciplines. Through practical learning, career guidance, and exposure to current tools and practices, SynergisticIT aims to help candidates prepare for the evolving demands of the technology workplace.\nAbout The Role\nSynergisticIT is seeking a motivated Software Developer to contribute to the design, development, testing, and maintenance of software applications. This opportunity is suited to candidates who enjoy solving problems, learning new technologies, and collaborating with others to deliver dependable software. You will work with development teams to understand requirements, implement features, investigate issues, and improve application quality. Depending on project needs, work may involve web applications, backend services, databases, APIs, or cloud-based solutions.\nThe ideal candidate demonstrates a strong foundation in programming and a genuine interest in developing production-ready skills. You should be comfortable learning unfamiliar frameworks, receiving feedback, and communicating progress clearly. Project assignments, technologies, and work arrangements may vary according to business and client requirements.\nQualifications\nApplicants should have a bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent education and practical experience. Familiarity with one or more programming languages, such as Java, Python, JavaScript, C#, or similar, is expected. Candidates should understand fundamental concepts including data structures, object-oriented programming, algorithms, and software development life cycles.\nKnowledge of relational databases and SQL is beneficial. Exposure to version control tools such as Git, software testing, REST APIs, web technologies, or cloud platforms is also valued. Candidates should be analytical, organized, and able to explain technical ideas clearly. A willingness to learn, respond constructively to feedback, and work effectively both independently and as part of a team is essential. Professional experience may be helpful but is not required for every opportunity.\nResponsibilities\nDesign, develop, test, and maintain application features in accordance with project requirements and established engineering practices. Review technical specifications, clarify requirements with stakeholders, and break assignments into manageable tasks. Write readable, maintainable code and participate in code reviews to support quality, consistency, and knowledge sharing.\nIdentify, troubleshoot, and resolve software defects while documenting findings and solutions. Create or update unit tests and other testing materials to help verify application behavior. Collaborate with developers, testers, designers, product teams, and other stakeholders throughout the development cycle. Use version control and project tracking tools to manage changes and communicate progress. Contribute to technical documentation and offer ideas for improving development processes, application performance, reliability, and user experience. Protect confidential information and follow applicable security, privacy, and client requirements.\nBenefits\nBenefits and employment terms may vary based on position, work location, client assignment, and eligibility. Depending on the applicable arrangement, opportunities may include professional development support, technical learning resources, career guidance, and experience working with current technologies. Eligible employees may also have access to company-sponsored benefits in accordance with the relevant plan documents and policies. Specific compensation, benefits, and work arrangements will be shared during the hiring process.\nEqual Opportunity\nSynergisticIT is committed to fair and inclusive employment practices. Employment decisions are based on job-related qualifications, skills, experience, and business needs. Applicants are considered without regard to legally protected characteristics under applicable law. Candidates who require a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process may contact the appropriate recruiting representative to discuss their needs.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4318354760": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T18:05:03.936755+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Are you passionate about creating robust and scalable software solutions?\nJoin us as a Full Stack Developer and play a key role in building impactful applications. We’re looking for someone with a strong technical background, problem-solving mindset, and collaborative attitude to help shape our innovative projects.\nResponsibilities\nDesign, develop, and implement scalable software applications using C# and .NET Core.\nBuild and optimize Web APIs with a focus on best practices.\nWork with JavaScript, jQuery, and other front-end technologies to deliver seamless user experiences.\nWrite clean, efficient, and maintainable code with a focus on performance and scalability.\nCollaborate with developers, product managers, and stakeholders to deliver new features and enhancements.\nTroubleshoot, debug and upgrade the software to ensure optimal functionality.\nLead by example, providing technical guidance and mentorship to the team.\nQualifications\nEducation: Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Science or a related field.\nExperience: 2 years of hands-on experience in software development, including front-end and back-end work.\nTechnical Skills:\nStrong expertise in C#, .NET Core, MVC, and Microservices architecture.\nProficiency in JavaScript, jQuery, and other front-end frameworks.\nKnowledge of database management and integration.\nSoft Skills:\nExcellent verbal and written communication skills.\nStrong analytical, problem-solving, and organizational abilities.\nA collaborative team player with a proactive attitude.\nWhy Join Us?\nCompetitive salary and comprehensive benefits.\nPerformance bonuses based on your contributions and team achievements.\nThe opportunity to work on industry-leading projects.\nLocation: This is a full-time, onsite role based in Karachi.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4447985754": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T18:05:03.936755+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Company Description\nAir is the leader in Enterprise Readiness. Our mission is to establish readiness as a real-time condition that is continuously achieved. Today, a dangerous Readiness Gap exists between what the front line needs and what is delivered. Our AI-native platform, Air Enterprise Readiness, aligns development, production, delivery, and sustainment into one coordinated execution system for government agencies and industrial suppliers. By revealing true capacity, exposing real constraints, coordinating resources, and executing at the speed of operational demands, the front line gets what it needs to succeed.\nJob Description\nWe are seeking self-starting, customer-value-oriented software engineers to join our Forward Deployed Engineering team. As a Forward Deployed Software Engineer at Air, you are accountable for building new and differentiated 0-to-1 capabilities, in the field with our customers, end to end. You are motivated by moving quickly but responsibly against urgent and compelling opportunities to deliver valuable software-driven outcomes to our customers. The idea of building something new energizes you and want to work on problems that matter, and you want to own. You understand and appreciate the value of face-to-face interactions with end users, and constantly seek to push the boundaries of what is possible.\nIn order to do this job well, you must be a curious and eager problem solver. You must possess exceptional judgment when it comes to balancing competing priorities and making tradeoffs. You must be flexible, you must value outcomes over process, you must thrive in ambiguous environments, and above all else focus on solving valuable problems for our customers.\nIn a typical week, the individual who fills this position could expect to:\nSpend the day onsite with users, listening to problems and asking questions seeking to understand pain points\nCollaborate with product managers and designers to scope, architect, and deliver 0-to-1 product initiatives and prototypes.\nBuild and deliver working, customer-facing prototypes.\nAssess, prioritize, and correct the most important gaps in prototype solutions under development based on user feedback and in partnership with product managers\nFail often, iterate quickly, and try again\nThis role is a full-time position located out of our office in Arlington, VA, Pittsburgh, PA, or Remote.\nThis role may require up to 50% travel.\nScope of Responsibilities\nConduct customer site visits to diagnose and understand pain points\nParticipate in the end-to-end software development of new feature functionality and design capabilities\nIterate quickly to progressively unlock customer value\nCraft clean, testable, and maintainable code\nQualifications\nU.S. Citizenship is required\nRequired Skills\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or related field, or equivalent work experience\n1+ years of front-end or back-end software development experience (SQL, Java and/or Typescript/React)\nAbility to work independently with little supervision\nA burning desire to work in a challenging, fast-paced tech environment\nDesired Skills\nCurrent possession of a U.S. security clearance or the ability to obtain one with our sponsorship\nExperience in or exposure to the nuances of a startup or other entrepreneurial environment\nExperience working within the boundaries of a federally accredited software environment\nExperience in or exposure to the nuances of a startup or other entrepreneurial environment\nExperience working in a customer-facing or consulting role\nWe firmly believe that past performance is the best indicator of future performance. If you thrive while building solutions to complex problems, are a self-starter, and are passionate about making an impact in global security, we’re eager to hear from you.\nAir is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability and protected veterans status or any other characteristic protected by law.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4466443420": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T18:05:03.936755+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Reddit is a community of communities. It's built on shared interests, passion, and trust, and is home to the most open and authentic conversations on the internet. Every day, Reddit users submit, vote, and comment on the topics they care most about. With 100,000+ active communities and approximately 130 million daily active unique visitors, Reddit is one of the internet's largest sources of information. For more information, visit www.redditinc.com.\nWe are seeking a Software Engineer to help us build the next version of media web experience. In this role, you will define the work on the technical components of how we deliver video and audio content at Reddit. Specifically, you will focus on our web media player and the APIs that power it, drawing on industry patterns from top streaming platforms to build seamless, low-latency playback experiences and interactive tools for creators and users alike.\nKey Responsibilities\nWork cross-functionally with product, design, and other engineering counterparts to execute on product and business strategy and build novel products and features that our users will love.\nContribute to the full development cycle: technical design, development, test, experimentation, analysis, and launch.\nDesign and implement end-to-end fullstack solutions, optimizing web UI components for our media player (React, TypeScript) and the backend APIs (Go, Python) that power them.\nMove fast while balancing quality. We can't afford extensive processes, and we also can't afford show-stopping bugs.\nYou'll be reviewing code and design docs, giving feedback on product specs and mocks.\nCollaborate with client engineers and platform engineers to improve performance of media across Reddit to serve better content globally.\nContribute to standards that improve developer workflows, recommend best practices, and help mentor junior engineers on the team to grow their technical expertise.\nQualifications\nBS degree in Computer Science, a similar technical field of study or equivalent practical experience.\n3+ years of software development experience in one or more general-purpose programming languages; Go, Python, Rust, Ruby.\nProficiency in modern web development technologies (JavaScript, React, Next.js, TypeScript) and experience translating complex UI/UX designs into scalable web applications.\nExperienced with GraphQL, REST, HTTP, gRPC, Thrift basics, and the ability to design and implement maintainable APIs.\nStrong organizational skills, the ability to prioritize tasks and to deliver projects on schedule.\nExcellent communication skills. You collaborate effectively with teams in a fully remote environment and discuss complex topics with technical and non-technical audiences.\nBenefits\nComprehensive Healthcare Benefits and Income Replacement Programs\n401k with Employer Match\nGlobal Benefit programs that fit your lifestyle, from workspace to professional development to caregiving support\nFamily Planning Support\nGender-Affirming Care\nMental Health & Coaching Benefits\nFlexible Vacation & Paid Volunteer Time Off\nGenerous Paid Parental Leave\nPay Transparency:\nThis job posting may span more than one career level.\nIn addition to base salary, this job is eligible to receive equity in the form of restricted stock units, and depending on the position offered, it may also be eligible to receive a commission. Additionally, Reddit offers a wide range of benefits to U.S.-based employees, including medical, dental, and vision insurance, 401(k) program with employer match, generous time off for vacation, and parental leave. To learn more, please visit https://www.redditinc.com/careers/.\nTo provide greater transparency to candidates, we share base salary ranges for all US-based job postings regardless of state. We set standard base pay ranges for all roles based on function, level, and country location, benchmarked against similar stage growth companies. Final offer amounts are determined by multiple factors including, skills, depth of work experience and relevant licenses/credentials, and may vary from the amounts listed below.\nThe base salary range for this position is:\n$165,000—$229,000 USD\nIn select roles and locations, the interviews will be recorded, transcribed and summarized by artificial intelligence (AI). You will have the opportunity to opt out of recording, transcription and summarization prior to any scheduled interviews.\nDuring the interview, we will collect the following categories of personal information: Identifiers, Professional and Employment-Related Information, Sensory Information (audio/video recording), and any other categories of personal information you choose to share with us. We will use this information to evaluate your application for employment or an independent contractor role, as applicable. We will not sell your personal information or disclose it to any third party for their marketing purposes. We will delete any recording of your interview promptly after making a hiring decision. For more information about how we will handle your personal information, including our retention of it, please refer to our Candidate Privacy Policy for Potential Employees and Contractors.\nReddit is proud to be an equal opportunity employer, and is committed to building a workforce representative of the diverse communities we serve. Reddit is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities and disabled veterans in our job application procedures. If, due to a disability, you need an accommodation during the interview process, please let your recruiter know.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4468818625": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T18:05:03.936755+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Senior Full-Stack Software Engineer\nCompensation: $170,000-$200,000+10% Bonus and full-time benefits/PTO\nLocation: 100% Remote\nWe are a market-leading, fast-growing event ticketing technology company. We use industry-leading technologies to solve complex challenges in a rapidly expanding global market — and we're looking for talented engineers who want to build things that matter.\nWe're a people-first culture that values engineering excellence, continuous growth, and giving individuals the freedom and ownership to create their own success. If you're driven by hard problems, great teammates, and work that genuinely impacts customers, we'd love to hear from you.\nWhat You'll Bring\nTechnical Skills\n- Comfortable working across multiple of the following: JavaScript, TypeScript, Node.js, Express, React, React Native, Expo, Vue, Vite, CSS, Redis, and Docker.\n- Solid experience with APIs, cloud infrastructure (AWS), SOA, SaaS architecture, messaging systems, stream processing, and SQL data stores.\n- Ability to read, evaluate, and reason about complex SQL — including query optimization and data structure analysis.\n- Familiarity with containerization and scaling of SaaS platform services.\n- Working knowledge of functional programming principles and software analysis techniques.\nEngineering Mindset\n- Experience building and launching new products from concept to market.\n- Comfortable using AI-assisted development tools (e.g., Copilot, Cursor, Claude Code) to accelerate workflows — including code review, technical planning, and implementation scaffolding — while maintaining full ownership and accountability over code quality and correctness.\n- Passionate about solving the right problems, in the right way, at the right time.\n- Equally comfortable giving and receiving feedback, and consistently demonstrates growth in their craft.\nWhat You'll Do\n- Translate business strategy and operating models into long-term technical product strategy using gap analysis and forward-looking architectural thinking.\n- Ensure technical capabilities — both product and platform — align with evolving business needs and goals.\n- Communicate goals, metrics, and value propositions clearly across the Engineering organization.\n- Drive design, development, and support of new and existing products in close collaboration with cross-functional stakeholders.\n- Mentor and support team members working through complex use cases and system design challenges, while leading technical change and transformation.\n- Deep-dive into applications and data stores to surface meaningful insights: profiling, tracing, operational intelligence, customer experience visualizations, and proactive trend analyses.\nQualifications\n- 5–10 solid years in engineering, product, or technical delivery (depth matters more than the number)\nEducation:\n- BS in Computer Science, IT, or related field",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4475045317": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T18:05:03.936755+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About FullStack\nFullStack is your AI-native engineering partner, built to turn AI capability into certainty. Most companies can demo AI; few can get it to production and prove what it produced. We close that gap with three capabilities, AI built into your products from the start, elite vetted talent who apply it, and transparent execution that shows value every step of the way. With now over 600 customers in North America, FullStack is one integrated partner for all your AI engineering needs. With FullStack, you move forward with confidence.\nWe’re Most Proud Of\nOffering life-changing career opportunities to talented software professionals across the Americas.\nBuilding highly-skilled software development teams for hundreds of the world’s greatest companies.\nHaving delivered hundreds of successful custom software solutions, which have positively impacted the lives and careers of millions of users.\nOur 4.1-star rating on GlassDoor.\nOur client Net Promoter Score of 68, twice the industry average.\nThe Opportunity\nJoin our talent network and connect with U.S. clients for flexible, project-based development work as an Agentic Software Engineer (Google Antigravity).\nYou will integrate directly into our client's team and work alongside their existing designers and engineers on a daily basis.\nWhat We're Looking For\n5+ years of professional software development experience with a deep understanding of full-stack architectures (e.g., Java, Python, C#, React, Node, etc.).\n1-3 years of professional experience using Google Antigravity as a primary development environment to coordinate AI-driven implementation across large, multi-file systems while maintaining architectural oversight.\nExperience delivering production software where AI systems generate the majority of implementation code.\nStrong context engineering skills, including structuring codebases, specifications, and documentation to produce reliable, context-efficient AI output.\nAbility to translate complex product requirements into machine-executable, AI-friendly specifications.\nExperience designing AI-first development workflows from specification through deployment.\nAbility to systematically improve AI-generated output through structured iteration and feedback loops.\nComfort working across multiple stacks, using AI to deliver high-quality, production-ready systems.\nExperience operating across frontend, backend, and infrastructure in AI-accelerated environments.\nDisciplined human-in-the-loop review practices, with risk-adjusted validation for high-impact or safety-critical flows.\nStrong curiosity and initiative in evaluating and adopting emerging AI-native engineering practices.\nAdvanced understanding of Agile methodologies and Lean principles and participation in team ceremonies as well as asynchronous work.\nAdvanced English is required.\nSuccessful completion of a four-year college degree is required.\nA positive mindset and a can-do attitude.\nAbility to identify with the goals of FullStack's clients and dedicate yourself to delivering on commitments.\nAbility to consistently work 40 hours per week.\nWork Authorization Requirements\nApplicants must be currently authorized to work in the country of this job posting on a full-time basis.\nFullStack will not sponsor applicants for work visas now or in the future.\nWhat We Offer\nCompetitive pay.\n100% remote work.\nThe ability to work with leading startups and Fortune 500 companies.\nContinuing education opportunities.\nOpportunity to grow and expand your career.\nOur talent network is committed to fostering a diverse, inclusive, and accessible environment where IT professionals can find opportunities that match their skills. We welcome individuals of all races, religions, genders, sexual orientations, national origins, abilities, and experiences. Our focus is on connecting talent with projects based on qualifications, ensuring a fair and transparent process that values diverse perspectives and global collaboration.\nLearn more about our Applicants Privacy Notice.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
