      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484100530": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T18:05:03.936755+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Project Description\nHiredbuddy is seeking an entry-level Full Stack Developer to join our remote team. You'll build and maintain web applications, collaborate with cross-functional teams, and grow your skills in a supportive environment. If you're passionate about coding and ready to make an impact, apply today!\nFull Description\nAs an Entry Level Full Stack Developer at Hiredbuddy, you will be an integral part of our engineering team, contributing to the design, development, and maintenance of web applications that serve a diverse client base. This remote role is perfect for someone who is eager to apply foundational coding skills in a real-world environment while learning from experienced professionals. You will work on both front-end and back-end components, ensuring seamless user experiences and robust server-side logic.\nKey Responsibilities\nDevelop and maintain responsive web applications using modern JavaScript frameworks such as React or Vue.js for the front end.\nBuild and integrate RESTful APIs and microservices using Node.js, Express, or similar back-end technologies.\nWrite clean, maintainable, and well-documented code that follows industry best practices.\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams including designers, product managers, and other developers to deliver high-quality features.\nParticipate in code reviews, provide constructive feedback, and continuously improve development processes.\nTroubleshoot and debug applications to optimize performance and ensure reliability.\nWork with databases (SQL or NoSQL) to design schemas, write queries, and manage data storage.\nUse version control systems like Git for collaborative development and deployment.\nStay updated with emerging technologies and suggest improvements to existing systems.\nAssist in testing and deployment using CI/CD pipelines and cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, or Heroku).\nTechnologies and Tools Our stack evolves, but currently we rely on:\nFront-end: HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript (ES6+), React, Redux, or Vue.js\nBack-end: Node.js, Express, Python (Django/Flask) or Ruby on Rails\nDatabases: PostgreSQL, MongoDB, or MySQL\nVersion Control: Git, GitHub/GitLab\nDeployment: Docker, AWS, Netlify, Vercel\nTesting: Jest, Mocha, Chai, Cypress\nCommunication: Slack, Zoom, Jira, Trello\nGrowth and Development At Hiredbuddy, we invest in our team's growth. You will receive direct mentorship from senior engineers, regular feedback, and access to resources that help you advance your skills. We encourage exploration of new tools and technologies, and we provide a clear path for progression to mid-level and senior roles. Your contributions will directly impact the success of our products and the satisfaction of our clients.\nWork Environment This is a fully remote position, allowing you to work from anywhere within the United States. We value work-life balance and flexibility, while maintaining a strong sense of community through virtual events, pair programming sessions, and open communication channels. You will have the support you need to succeed, whether it's through structured onboarding, regular check-ins, or a dedicated buddy system.\nIf you are ready to launch your career as a Full Stack Developer and make a meaningful impact, we would love to hear from you.\nRequirements\n0-2 years of experience in full stack development (internships and personal projects count)\nProficiency in at least one front-end framework (React, Vue, or Angular) and one back-end language (Node.js, Python, or Ruby)\nUnderstanding of RESTful APIs and HTTP fundamentals\nFamiliarity with relational and/or NoSQL databases\nKnowledge of version control systems (Git)\nAbility to write clean, testable code\nStrong problem-solving skills and attention to detail\nExcellent communication and teamwork abilities\nSelf-motivated and able to work independently in a remote environment\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field (or equivalent experience)\nBenefits\nCompetitive entry-level salary with performance reviews\n100% remote work flexibility\nHealth, dental, and vision insurance\nPaid time off and public holidays\nHome office stipend\nAccess to learning platforms and certification courses\nMentorship from senior developers\nOpportunity for career growth and role advancement",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484442793": {
