      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484472661": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T18:05:03.936755+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About the Company\nKarias Health is a health benefits platform that combines self-funded healthcare financing with a consumer-focused, AI-enabled navigation ecosystem. The company integrates health coverage, cost containment strategies, concierge support, and proprietary technology to make healthcare simpler, more transparent, predictable, and cost-effective.\nKarias Health focuses on helping employers manage healthcare costs, giving members greater clarity when navigating care, and enabling brokers to serve as strategic partners. Through data and technology, the company aims to improve member experiences while supporting access to high-value care.\nAbout the Role\nKarias Health is seeking a Senior Software Engineer to help build AI-powered healthcare products that reduce costs, improve member care, and scale across self-funded employer health plans. This is a foundational engineering position for a US-based professional who will help define the architecture of the company's next-generation, white-label platform.\nReporting to the Lead Engineer and working closely with the Chief Product and Technology Officer (CPTO), the Senior Software Engineer will take ownership of architectural decisions, establish engineering standards, and mentor offshore engineers while remaining actively involved in development. The role is approximately 80% hands-on engineering and 20% technical leadership.\nThe successful candidate will also help establish safe and effective AI-assisted development practices across specification, implementation, testing, and code review, with particular attention to the requirements of a regulated healthcare environment.\nKey Responsibilities\nAssess the existing codebase and infrastructure, documenting recommendations on what should be retained or replaced for the white-label platform.\nDefine and document the platform architecture, including the multi-tenant model, data isolation approach, and per-tenant configuration.\nDevelop and maintain production applications using Ruby on Rails, Python, and AWS services.\nMake architectural decisions within an established Ruby on Rails codebase, including tenancy scoping, large-scale database migrations, and service boundaries.\nBuild the technical foundation for the planned early-2027 enterprise launch.\nMentor offshore engineers and establish standards for code quality, development practices, and technical delivery.\nServe as a technical point of accountability for the quality and reliability of platform releases.\nApply AI-assisted development tools across specifications, implementation, test generation, and code review.\nEstablish appropriate safeguards for AI-assisted engineering within a regulated environment.\nWork with the Lead Engineer and CPTO to guide platform direction and align technical decisions with business requirements.\nEstablish and improve engineering standards and CI/CD practices across the team.\nInitial Deliverables\nFirst 30 Days\nComplete an assessment of the existing codebase and infrastructure, with a written recommendation on what should carry forward into the white-label platform and what should not.\nFirst 60 Days\nDecide on and document the multi-tenancy model and data isolation approach, with agreement from the Lead Engineer and CPTO.\nGo-Live Preparation\nBuild the multi-tenant platform foundation and establish engineering standards and CI/CD practices with the engineering team.\nRequired Qualifications\nApproximately 7+ years of professional software engineering experience, with demonstrated ownership of architecture from design through implementation.\nProduction experience with Ruby on Rails, including working within mature codebases and making structural decisions involving tenancy scoping, large-scale migrations, and service boundaries.\nDemonstrated proficiency in AI-assisted development tools for specifications, implementation, testing, and code review, along with a considered approach to their appropriate use.\nStrong Python skills and production experience with AWS.\nDirect experience building multi-tenant SaaS platforms, including tenancy, data isolation, and per-tenant configuration decisions.\nPreferred Qualifications\nExperience with TypeScript and JavaScript frameworks.\nTechnical leadership experience, including mentoring engineers, establishing standards, and conducting code reviews while remaining hands-on.\nExperience in healthcare, fintech, or another regulated industry where compliance requirements influence architecture.\nExperience delivering LLM-powered product features to real users.\nExperience working with distributed or offshore engineering teams.\nFamiliarity with HIPAA and SOC 2 requirements in a software development context.\nTechnical Stack\nRuby on Rails\nPython\nAWS, including RDS, S3, Redshift, Glue, and OpenSearch\nRetrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipelines using HIPAA-eligible large language models (LLMs)\nEmployment Type and Work Arrangement\nPosition: Senior Software Engineer\nDepartment: Platform Engineering\nEmployment Type: Full-time\nWork Arrangement: Fully remote within the United States\nReports To: Lead Engineer\nThe role requires attendance at approximately one to two team gatherings per quarter.\nCompensation and Benefits\nCompetitive compensation.\nComprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their dependents.\nA mission-driven culture focused on trust, excellence, and service.\nThe opportunity to build and scale technology within a high-growth startup.\nAutonomy, flexibility, and the ability to directly influence business outcomes.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
