      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/moritzbaierlentz_game-studio-funding-is-back-gardens-interactive-share-7513608118791196673-sNWA": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:29:49.057015+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Game studio funding is back: Gardens Interactive has raised a $35M+ Series B, bringing total funding to over $70M before launching its flagship game.\n\nLed by Lightspeed, the round includes Sequoia Capital, Index Ventures, Accel, Eric Schmidt’s Innovation Endeavors, the Nintendo family (Yamauchi No.10), the ZeniMax Media family (James Altman), and the founders of Slack and OpenAI's Sora.\n\nBy any measure, but certainly in 2026, that's an extraordinary vote of confidence and tier-1 syndicate for a pre-launch studio. What inspires that conviction while it seems all venture dollars chase automation?\n\nA team creating a new genre around a simple and proven design principle: deepen human connections, and let the players be the fun.\n\nGardens calls it a “strandbox”: a social roleplaying world where chance encounters become adventures, players shape each other’s stories, and your actions leave something behind for whoever comes next.\n\nFrom serial game-of-the-year creators behind Journey and Sky, the team blends indie creativity and beautiful art with an ambitious AAA live-ops platform bet on how games can create significant and long-lasting emotional encounters.\n\nThis one is deeply personal. I love Stephen, 🔔Chris, and Lexie like brothers. After serving on Gardens’ board for the past three years, I’m rejoining as a personal investor and advisor, doubling down with my own capital and time. To continue an extraordinary development journey that already brought so many wonderful once-strangers together.\n\nI can’t wait for you all to play what they’re building.\n\nBloomberg exclusive by Cecilia D'Anastasio: https://lnkd.in/dYJ4Xj9C",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-07T14:36:12.326Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/paulcopplestone_today-supabase-is-announcing-150m-in-new-share-7511811435921072128-6ltf": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T22:29:49.057015+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Today, Supabase is announcing $150M in new funding, led by GIC, with CapitalG, IronArc Ventures, and Square Peg participating. We’re also welcoming Turso to Supabase.\n\nThe past year has been the fastest period of growth in Supabase’s history. We’re now adding more than 1M users and nearly 5M databases every month, and around 70% of new databases are being created by agents or AI-driven tools.\n\nAI is changing the economics of software creation. More people can build software, developers can build dramatically more of it, and agents are increasingly building alongside them.\n\nOur goal is to make Supabase the foundation for this agentic era. That means making it radically cheaper to start, while giving every application a clear path to scale.\nThat’s a big part of why we’re acquiring Turso.\n\nAs agents create more software, database demand will outpace the world’s current capacity. Turso has built an architecture that can handle vastly more small databases at a fraction of today’s cost. An agent can get an isolated database instantly, without requiring a dedicated machine for every workload.\n\nFor existing users, nothing changes. Supabase will continue building around Postgres, while Turso will continue its work on SQLite. Together, we’re creating something new that will bring the Supabase experience to every agent.\n\nThere’s a lot that brought our teams together: open source, developer experience, and a willingness to tackle hard infrastructure problems. We’re excited to welcome Glauber Costa , Pekka Enberg, and the entire Turso team to Supabase, with Glauber joining as Head of Agentic Services.\n\nThank you to GIC, CapitalG, IronArc, SquarePeg, and everyone who continues to support us. Most importantly, thank you to the Supabase community. You keep building faster than we expect, which means we have to keep doing the same.\n\nSri Muppidi has more on the news for the New York Times and we’ve shared more on the Supabase blog. Links in the comments.",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-02T15:36:49.683Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/asimahmood_nextjs-frontend-developer-location-karachi-activity-7450882245944385536-B1LW": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T18:08:30.712437+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Next.js Frontend Developer\nLocation: Karachi\n\nWe are looking for a skilled Next.js Frontend Developer to join our growing team. If you’re passionate about building fast, scalable, and user-friendly web applications, we’d love to hear from you!\n\nKey Responsibilities:\nDevelop and maintain web applications using Next.js and React.js\nBuild reusable, efficient, and scalable frontend components\nOptimize applications for maximum speed and performance\nCollaborate with backend developers and designers\nEnsure responsiveness across devices and browsers\n\nRequirements:\nProven experience with Next.js and React.js\nStrong grip on JavaScript (ES6+), HTML5, CSS3\nExperience with API integration (REST/GraphQL)\nFamiliarity with version control (Git)\nUnderstanding of SEO and web performance optimization\nGood problem-solving and communication skills\nExposure to POS or eCommerce solutions\n\nApply Now: Share your profile at jobs@imtiaz.com.pk, mentioning “Next.js Developer” in the subject line",
          "posted_at": "2026-04-17T12:25:58.105Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/china-produces-about-85-of-the-worlds-cathode-share-7516513337908633600-8_eD": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T18:08:30.712437+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "China produces about 85% of the world's cathode active material. The West needs new battery chemistries to compete, but traditional R&D can take years to deliver them. \n \nToday, we announced $45M in funding to change that. \n \nBacked by  Zone II Ventures, and Course Corrected, we're scaling our AI-powered Discovery Engine, which combines 18 years of proprietary battery data with automated labs that physically build and test new materials. Over these 18 years our platform has run more than 225 projects for more than 85 customers across the battery value chain, including nearly a dozen Fortune 500 companies, and has resulted in more than 100 battery patents.  Along the way, the platform generated an internally consistent dataset covering more than 500,000 physical cells tested at over 165 million cycles.  \n \nOur technology has already helped deliver DRX, a new family of nickel- and cobalt-free cathode materials designed to reduce dependence on China. Now, we're bringing DRX toward commercialization while using AI to accelerate the next generation of breakthroughs. \n \nLed by founder and CEO Mathias Ingvarsson, COO and former Tesla manufacturing leader Steven Prast, and Chief Scientific Officer Dee Strand, we're building a faster path from battery discovery to commercial deployment. \n \nRead more in Fortune by Nick Lichtenberg. Article link in the first comment.",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-15T15:00:30.119Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/exaltia-offical_were-hiring-mern-nextjs-developer-activity-7382347710131056640-aPen": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T18:08:30.712437+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "🚀 We’re Hiring: MERN / Next.js Developer\n📍 Location: On-site – Karachi\n 🕓 Timings: Mon–Fri: 9 AM–5 PM | Sat: 9 AM–2 PM\n 💼 Type: Full-time | Experience: 1–2 years\n\nResponsibilities\nDevelop web apps using MERN Stack and Next.js\nBuild & integrate RESTful APIs\nCollaborate with team using Git/GitHub\nDebug, optimize, and deploy apps (Vercel/PM2)\n\nRequirements\n1–2 years experience in MERN/Next.js projects\nStrong in React, Node.js, Express, MongoDB\nFamiliar with MySQL/PostgreSQL (plus point)\nProblem-solving mindset\nMust have 1 demo/live project\n\nPerks\nLearning & mentorship from senior devs\nLive project exposure\nCareer growth & performance bonuses\n\n📩 Apply Now:\n Send CV + Portfolio to\n 📧 hr@webexaltia.com\n | 📱 +92 370 2865556\nOnly shortlisted candidates will be contacted.",
          "posted_at": "2025-10-10T09:34:11.458Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/heykristopher_xbox-is-building-a-new-kind-of-flywheel-with-ugcPost-7513955395246161920-7a3g": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T18:08:30.712437+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "XBOX is building a new kind of flywheel with games at the center.\n\nThe company announced XP this morning (a clever title)—a new division headed by Kayleen Walters focused on creating more on-ramps for fans to its beloved IP through film & television, consumer products, live events, and strategic partnerships.\n\nHere are the four divisions:\n\n* XBOX PICTURES: Bringing our worlds and characters to new audiences through film, television, and other forms of linear storytelling. \n* XBOX PRODUCTS: Creating products that are authentic to the fandom that allow fans to celebrate and express the franchises they love. \n* XBOX PLACES: Bringing communities together through live events, immersive experiences, attractions, broadcasts, and destinations. \n* XBOX PARTNERSHIPS: Working with creators, brands, and communities to develop new experiences, sponsorships, and brand partnerships.\n\nThe move—championed by Matthew Ball following an internal memo from Asha Sharma—is both elegant and strategic. It adopts the best strategies from Disney and Nintendo, both of whom understand that content is king. Where Disney’s flywheel was built strategically around film and television firs, Nintendo’s is game first.\n\nWith this move, XBOX is positioning itself to move beyond being a mere platform to owning its market position as both a publisher and steward of massive IP (from Minecraft to Halo and beyond).\n\nI’m excited to see where this leads.",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-08T13:36:09.005Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/karachi-jobsz_hiring-full-stack-web-developer-key-responsibilities-activity-7495034246613573632-U4Tb": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T18:08:30.712437+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Hiring: Full-Stack Web Developer\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\nDevelop modern, responsive web applications using React.js / Next.js\nBuild scalable backend services and RESTful / GraphQL APIs (Node.js or Python/FastAPI)\nIntegrate AI/ML model APIs and manage inference endpoints\nDesign and maintain relational and NoSQL databases (PostgreSQL, MongoDB)\nSet up and maintain CI/CD pipelines (GitHub Actions, Docker, Kubernetes)\nDeploy and manage cloud infrastructure on AWS, GCP, or Azure\nImplement authentication, authorization, and security best practices\nMonitor application performance, uptime, and optimize for Core Web Vitals\nUse AI app builders (Lovable, Replit, v0) to rapidly prototype and scaffold new web features\n\nRequirements:\n\n3+ years of full-stack web development experience\nProficiency in React.js and at least one backend framework (Node.js/Express or Python/FastAPI)\nSolid understanding of databases, data modeling, and query optimization\nExperience with containerization (Docker) and basic Kubernetes orchestration\nFamiliarity with cloud services: storage, serverless functions, and managed databases\nUnderstanding of web security: OWASP Top 10, OAuth 2.0, JWT\nDemonstrated hands-on proficiency with AI development tools: Claude, Gemini, ChatGPT, Cursor, Lovable, and Replit — portfolio evidence required\n\nLocation: Korangi Industrial Area, Karachi.\nApply now by sending your CV to: hr.talent@ideas.com.pk",
          "posted_at": "2026-08-17T08:30:15.340Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/karachi-jobsz_were-hiring-web-developer-frontend-php-activity-7476920524120604672-0VQx": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-30T18:08:30.712437+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "We're Hiring: Web Developer (Frontend + PHP / Next.js)\n\nPARADIGM DIGITAL SOLUTIONS (PVT) LTD is looking for a skilled Web Developer to build, maintain, and keep our websites running in top shape.\n\nIf you write clean code, care about performance, and like owning a site end-to-end, we'd love to hear from you.\n\nWhat we're looking for:\nStrong hands-on experience with HTML and CSS\nSolid PHP development skills\nProven experience with Next.js (and React, which it's built on)\nExperience with site health management diagnosing and fixing technical issues, performance monitoring, and general upkeep\nAttention to detail and a problem-solving mindset\nAbility to work independently and meet deadlines\n\n📍 Location: DMCHS, Karachi (Onsite)\n🕘 Shift Timing: 8:00 PM – 5:00 AM\n🏢 Job Type: Onsite, Full-time\n\nSend your resume and portfolio to hr@paradigmdigitals.com",
          "posted_at": "2026-06-28T08:52:47.387Z"
        }
      },
